1
00:00:34,118 --> 00:00:36,912
Start simple.
Start with what you know is true.

2
00:00:38,497 --> 00:00:42,042
My name is Katniss Everdeen.
My home is District 12.

3
00:00:42,668 --> 00:00:45,379
I was in the Hunger Games. I escaped.

4
00:00:46,005 --> 00:00:49,550
Peeta... Peeta was left behind.

5
00:00:53,637 --> 00:00:55,055
Miss Everdeen?

6
00:00:56,182 --> 00:00:57,516
You can't be in here.

7
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:01,395
I had a nightmare. Just five more minutes.

8
00:01:02,563 --> 00:01:06,358
You need to sleep. We can help you sleep.

9
00:01:07,735 --> 00:01:09,236
Just five more minutes.

10
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,113
No.

11
00:01:14,533 --> 00:01:16,243
No, please, don't. It's just five more...

12
00:01:16,285 --> 00:01:20,623
Don't touch me! Don't!
No! Get off of me!

13
00:02:17,763 --> 00:02:19,223
Finnick.

14
00:02:23,435 --> 00:02:26,730
I wanted to go back for Peeta and Johanna,

15
00:02:27,398 --> 00:02:31,443
but I couldn't move.

16
00:02:36,031 --> 00:02:39,160
They have Annie, too. They took her.

17
00:02:42,955 --> 00:02:46,792
She's in the Capitol.

18
00:02:51,005 --> 00:02:52,756
I wish she was dead.

19
00:02:55,134 --> 00:02:58,095
I wish they were all dead and we were, too.

20
00:03:27,917 --> 00:03:29,335
Miss Everdeen.

21
00:03:29,543 --> 00:03:32,421
Colonel Boggs,
District 13's head of security.

22
00:03:33,047 --> 00:03:34,423
I know you've been discharged,

23
00:03:34,465 --> 00:03:36,842
but President Coin's
requested to meet with you first.

24
00:03:37,134 --> 00:03:38,844
Is there any news?

25
00:03:39,011 --> 00:03:40,971
I'm just here to escort you.

26
00:04:12,878 --> 00:04:15,881
We were always told
there was nothing left of 13.

27
00:04:16,131 --> 00:04:18,550
Capitol bombed the surface to rubble.

28
00:04:19,927 --> 00:04:23,055
But we're military,
so we learned to survive down here.

29
00:04:23,806 --> 00:04:25,599
Preparing, training.

30
00:04:26,934 --> 00:04:28,310
The war never stopped for us.

31
00:05:00,426 --> 00:05:01,802
There she is.

32
00:05:02,428 --> 00:05:04,138
Our Girl on Fire.

33
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:08,142
Madam President, may I present you with
The Mockingjay.

34
00:05:08,225 --> 00:05:10,561
What an honor it is to meet you.

35
00:05:11,270 --> 00:05:12,604
You're a courageous young woman.

36
00:05:12,896 --> 00:05:15,357
I know how disorienting this must be.

37
00:05:15,858 --> 00:05:19,153
And I can't imagine what it's like to
live through the atrocities of those Games.

38
00:05:19,445 --> 00:05:22,448
Katniss, President Alma Coin.

39
00:05:23,282 --> 00:05:26,285
Please know how welcome you are.

40
00:05:26,618 --> 00:05:28,996
I hope you'll find some comfort with us.

41
00:05:29,246 --> 00:05:31,498
We've known loss in 13, too.

42
00:05:32,082 --> 00:05:36,670
This is history. Right here at this table.

43
00:05:36,712 --> 00:05:39,214
I apologize.
I wish you had more time to recover,

44
00:05:39,256 --> 00:05:41,133
but unfortunately, we
don't have that luxury.

45
00:05:41,175 --> 00:05:42,509
Please, have a seat.

46
00:05:43,594 --> 00:05:46,180
Are you aware of what's happened?

47
00:05:48,515 --> 00:05:51,310
When you fired your
arrow at the force field

48
00:05:52,144 --> 00:05:54,313
you electrified the nation.

49
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:59,193
There have been riots and uprisings
and strikes in seven districts.

50
00:05:59,777 --> 00:06:02,196
We believe that if we
keep this energy going

51
00:06:02,237 --> 00:06:04,907
we can unify the districts
against the Capitol.

52
00:06:05,157 --> 00:06:07,743
But if we don't, if we let it dissipate,

53
00:06:08,077 --> 00:06:10,871
we could be waiting another 75 years
for this opportunity.

54
00:06:11,163 --> 00:06:13,207
Everyone in 13 is ready for this.

55
00:06:13,290 --> 00:06:15,125
What about Peeta? Is he alive?

56
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:18,170
I don't know. And I wish that I did.

57
00:06:18,879 --> 00:06:22,299
But there's no way for me to contact
my operatives inside the Capitol.

58
00:06:22,341 --> 00:06:26,053
The Capitol has always suppressed
communication between the districts.

59
00:06:26,178 --> 00:06:30,891
But I know their system very well.
I managed to break through.

60
00:06:31,183 --> 00:06:33,227
All we need now is the perfect message.

61
00:06:33,477 --> 00:06:35,646
Katniss, here's what we need to do.

62
00:06:35,771 --> 00:06:38,524
We need to show them
that The Mockingjay's alive and well

63
00:06:38,565 --> 00:06:41,318
and willing to stand
up and join this fight.

64
00:06:41,944 --> 00:06:46,323
'Cause we need every district
to stand up to this Capitol.

65
00:06:46,532 --> 00:06:47,991
The way you did.

66
00:06:48,992 --> 00:06:53,872
So we're gonna shoot
a series of propaganda clips,

67
00:06:54,248 --> 00:06:57,084
propos, I like to call them,
on The Mockingjay.

68
00:06:57,543 --> 00:07:01,797
Spreads the word that we're
gonna stoke the fire of this rebellion.

69
00:07:02,131 --> 00:07:04,508
The fire that The Mockingjay started.

70
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:06,385
You left him there.

71
00:07:07,469 --> 00:07:10,347
You left Peeta in that arena to die.

72
00:07:10,389 --> 00:07:11,449
Katniss, there are so many...

73
00:07:11,473 --> 00:07:13,267
Peeta was the one
who was supposed to live.

74
00:07:13,308 --> 00:07:14,351
Miss Everdeen.

75
00:07:16,478 --> 00:07:21,150
This revolution is about everyone.
It's about all of us.

76
00:07:21,567 --> 00:07:22,943
And we need a voice.

77
00:07:24,153 --> 00:07:26,071
Then you should've saved Peeta.

78
00:07:34,872 --> 00:07:36,915
Maybe you should have
rescued the boy instead.

79
00:07:37,416 --> 00:07:38,625
No.

80
00:07:40,294 --> 00:07:44,548
No, listen to me.
No one else can do this but her.

81
00:07:44,590 --> 00:07:46,300
This is not the girl you described.

82
00:07:47,968 --> 00:07:50,596
Obviously, we need to make it personal.

83
00:07:50,929 --> 00:07:52,514
Remind her who the real enemy is.

84
00:07:52,556 --> 00:07:54,409
She knows who the enemy is.
That's not the issue.

85
00:07:54,433 --> 00:07:55,934
Unless she's forgotten.

86
00:07:57,352 --> 00:07:59,313
There's explaining and there's showing.

87
00:08:01,064 --> 00:08:03,400
Let her see what the Capitol did to 12.

88
00:08:03,775 --> 00:08:07,696
She can't handle it.
The Games destroyed her.

89
00:08:08,947 --> 00:08:10,949
This is the only choice you have.

90
00:08:11,783 --> 00:08:15,037
People don't always show up
the way you want them to, Madam President.

91
00:08:15,162 --> 00:08:17,915
But that anger, that anger-driven defiance,

92
00:08:17,956 --> 00:08:20,334
that's what we want.
And we can redirect it.

93
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,419
We need to unite these people out there

94
00:08:22,461 --> 00:08:25,547
that have been doing nothing but
killing each other in an arena for years.

95
00:08:25,964 --> 00:08:28,133
We have to have a lightning rod.

96
00:08:29,426 --> 00:08:32,512
They'll follow her.
She's the face of the revolution.

97
00:08:32,804 --> 00:08:34,723
Let her see it. Let her go home.

98
00:08:37,643 --> 00:08:38,852
Send her.

99
00:09:05,837 --> 00:09:07,677
I can't believe
you're going through with this.

100
00:09:09,174 --> 00:09:10,550
You can say "no."

101
00:09:10,801 --> 00:09:12,511
I need to see it for myself.

102
00:09:14,179 --> 00:09:15,389
This way.

103
00:10:12,237 --> 00:10:16,074
13 swept everything,
top to bottom so you'd be safe.

104
00:10:18,076 --> 00:10:20,203
You sure you don't want me to go with you?

105
00:10:20,829 --> 00:10:23,123
Yeah. I'm sure.

106
00:10:26,710 --> 00:10:28,879
We'll have our eyes on you from above.

107
00:13:59,297 --> 00:14:00,799
Figures.

108
00:14:04,219 --> 00:14:05,262
Hey!

109
00:14:06,429 --> 00:14:07,681
Come on.

110
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:11,142
Don't you wanna see Prim?

111
00:14:12,811 --> 00:14:15,021
There you go. You're breakin' my heart.

112
00:15:25,175 --> 00:15:26,676
Egeria!

113
00:15:30,513 --> 00:15:32,307
We need to fix these lines.

114
00:15:33,475 --> 00:15:35,435
I won't say "rebels."

115
00:15:36,061 --> 00:15:38,939
These are senseless acts of defiance.

116
00:15:39,272 --> 00:15:41,024
And I won't legitimize them.

117
00:15:42,525 --> 00:15:45,320
We'll call them "criminals."

118
00:15:48,448 --> 00:15:49,491
"Radicals."

119
00:15:52,369 --> 00:15:56,122
Otherwise we're breaking my oldest rule.

120
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:59,960
Never let them see you bleed.

121
00:16:02,712 --> 00:16:04,381
Citizens,

122
00:16:05,298 --> 00:16:10,220
tonight I address all of Panem as one.

123
00:16:11,471 --> 00:16:13,473
<i>Since the Dark Days,</i>

124
00:16:13,807 --> 00:16:17,477
<i>Panem has had
an unprecedented era of peace.</i>

125
00:16:18,019 --> 00:16:21,231
<i>It is a peace built upon cooperation.</i>

126
00:16:21,523 --> 00:16:24,401
<i>And a respect for law and order.</i>

127
00:16:25,777 --> 00:16:28,321
<i>In the past weeks,
you have heard of sporadic violence</i>

128
00:16:28,363 --> 00:16:33,326
<i>following the actions of a few radicals
in the Quarter Quell.</i>

129
00:16:34,077 --> 00:16:36,955
<i>Those who choose this destructive path,</i>

130
00:16:37,497 --> 00:16:39,999
<i>your actions are based on
a misunderstanding</i>

131
00:16:40,041 --> 00:16:43,628
<i>of how we have survived. Together.</i>

132
00:16:44,254 --> 00:16:46,214
<i>It is a contract.</i>

133
00:16:46,965 --> 00:16:52,012
<i>Each district supplies the Capitol.
Like blood to a heart.</i>

134
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:57,434
<i>In return,
the Capitol provides order and security.</i>

135
00:16:58,309 --> 00:17:00,228
<i>To refuse work</i>

136
00:17:01,021 --> 00:17:04,357
<i>is to put the entire system in danger.</i>

137
00:17:04,983 --> 00:17:08,361
<i>The Capitol is the beating heart of Panem.</i>

138
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:11,156
<i>Nothing can survive without a heart.</i>

139
00:17:12,824 --> 00:17:15,034
<i>The criminals that kneel before you</i>

140
00:17:16,119 --> 00:17:19,039
<i>use symbols for the purpose of sedition.</i>

141
00:17:19,581 --> 00:17:23,042
Which is why all images of The Mockingjay

142
00:17:23,126 --> 00:17:24,419
are now forbidden.

143
00:17:26,004 --> 00:17:28,590
Possessing them
will be considered treason.

144
00:17:29,049 --> 00:17:31,009
Punishable by death.

145
00:17:32,343 --> 00:17:34,888
Justice shall be served swiftly.

146
00:17:35,513 --> 00:17:38,058
<i>Order shall be restored.</i>

147
00:17:39,017 --> 00:17:41,978
<i>To those who ignore
the warnings of history,</i>

148
00:17:48,735 --> 00:17:52,781
<i>prepare to pay the ultimate price.</i>

149
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:40,912
It's okay. We're okay.

150
00:18:41,412 --> 00:18:42,914
We're all here now.

151
00:18:43,373 --> 00:18:44,457
Buttercup!

152
00:18:46,417 --> 00:18:47,961
I smuggled him in.

153
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:53,466
I got Dad.

154
00:18:57,053 --> 00:18:59,514
And I got some of your herbs
from the kitchen.

155
00:19:01,266 --> 00:19:03,309
They have strict rules.

156
00:19:03,726 --> 00:19:06,187
I don't know what they'll do
if they find him here.

157
00:19:21,244 --> 00:19:22,524
You should try to eat something.

158
00:19:36,509 --> 00:19:41,639
<i>Hello. Good evening.
And a big welcome to all in Panem.</i>

159
00:19:41,973 --> 00:19:43,474
<i>I'm Caesar Flickerman.</i>

160
00:19:43,641 --> 00:19:46,186
<i>And whoever you are,
whatever it is you're doing,</i>

161
00:19:46,227 --> 00:19:47,812
<i>if you're working, put down your work.</i>

162
00:19:47,979 --> 00:19:49,739
<i>If you're having dinner,
stop having dinner.</i>

163
00:19:49,981 --> 00:19:53,651
<i>Because you are going to
want to witness this tonight.</i>

164
00:19:54,485 --> 00:19:56,446
<i>There has been rampant speculation</i>

165
00:19:56,487 --> 00:19:59,866
<i>about what really happened
in the Quarter Quell.</i>

166
00:20:00,033 --> 00:20:04,495
<i>And here to shed a little light on the
subject for us is a very special guest.</i>

167
00:20:04,662 --> 00:20:08,374
<i>Please welcome Mr. Peeta Mellark.</i>

168
00:20:09,417 --> 00:20:14,672
<i>Peeta, a lot of people
feel as though they are in the dark.</i>

169
00:20:14,714 --> 00:20:16,841
<i>Yeah, I know how they feel.</i>

170
00:20:17,508 --> 00:20:19,052
<i>Now, so set the stage for us.</i>

171
00:20:19,093 --> 00:20:22,055
<i>Talk us through what really happened</i>

172
00:20:22,305 --> 00:20:24,682
<i>on that final and controversial night.</i>

173
00:20:24,974 --> 00:20:29,187
<i>First off, you have to understand
that when you're in the Games</i>

174
00:20:30,271 --> 00:20:33,024
<i>you only get one wish. It's very costly.</i>

175
00:20:33,107 --> 00:20:34,192
You're alive.

176
00:20:34,234 --> 00:20:35,318
<i>It costs your life.</i>

177
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:36,629
<i>I think it costs more than your life.</i>

178
00:20:36,653 --> 00:20:38,255
<i>How do you mean?
What's more than your life?</i>

179
00:20:38,279 --> 00:20:42,700
<i>I mean to murder innocent people,
that costs everything that you are.</i>

180
00:20:42,742 --> 00:20:43,910
<i>Yes.</i>

181
00:20:43,993 --> 00:20:47,121
<i>So you hold on to that one wish.</i>

182
00:20:47,872 --> 00:20:50,416
<i>And that night my wish was to save Katniss.</i>

183
00:20:50,458 --> 00:20:51,584
<i>Yes.</i>

184
00:20:51,918 --> 00:20:54,921
<i>I should've just run off with her
earlier in the day like she'd wanted.</i>

185
00:20:54,963 --> 00:20:59,634
<i>But you didn't. Why?
Were you caught up in Beetee's plan?</i>

186
00:21:00,218 --> 00:21:03,054
<i>No, I was caught up trying to play allies.</i>

187
00:21:03,805 --> 00:21:05,598
<i>And then they separated us</i>

188
00:21:07,892 --> 00:21:09,102
<i>and that's when I lost her.</i>

189
00:21:10,979 --> 00:21:12,689
<i>And then the lightning hit</i>

190
00:21:12,855 --> 00:21:16,609
<i>and the whole force field around the arena
just blew out.</i>

191
00:21:16,901 --> 00:21:21,656
<i>Yes, but, Peeta,
Katniss is the one who blew it out.</i>

192
00:21:21,698 --> 00:21:22,740
<i>No.</i>

193
00:21:22,782 --> 00:21:23,783
<i>You saw the footage.</i>

194
00:21:23,825 --> 00:21:26,119
<i>No, she didn't know what she was doing.</i>

195
00:21:26,244 --> 00:21:29,956
<i>Neither of us knew there was
a bigger plan going on. We had no idea.</i>

196
00:21:29,998 --> 00:21:31,124
<i>- You had no idea?
- No.</i>

197
00:21:31,165 --> 00:21:35,962
<i>All right. Well, Peeta, there are many
who find this suspicious to say the least.</i>

198
00:21:36,045 --> 00:21:40,091
<i>It seems as though
she was part of a rebel plan.</i>

199
00:21:40,425 --> 00:21:43,511
<i>Do you think it was part of her plan
to be almost killed by Johanna?</i>

200
00:21:44,262 --> 00:21:46,848
<i>Or part of the plan
to be paralyzed by lightning?</i>

201
00:21:47,015 --> 00:21:51,311
<i>No, we were not part of any rebel plan.
We had no idea what was going on.</i>

202
00:21:51,561 --> 00:21:55,314
<i>All right. I believe you, Peeta Mellark.
Thank you.</i>

203
00:21:55,356 --> 00:21:56,399
<i>Yeah.</i>

204
00:21:56,441 --> 00:21:58,735
<i>And I was going to ask you to speak
about the unrest</i>

205
00:21:58,776 --> 00:22:01,112
<i>but I think you might be too upset.</i>

206
00:22:01,362 --> 00:22:02,613
<i>No, I can.</i>

207
00:22:02,655 --> 00:22:04,449
<i>- Are you sure?
- Absolutely.</i>

208
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:05,658
<i>Thank you.</i>

209
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:14,000
<i>I want everyone who's watching to stop</i>

210
00:22:14,125 --> 00:22:17,295
<i>and to think about
what a civil war could mean.</i>

211
00:22:17,503 --> 00:22:19,672
<i>We almost went extinct once before.</i>

212
00:22:19,964 --> 00:22:21,841
<i>And now our numbers are even fewer.</i>

213
00:22:21,883 --> 00:22:22,884
He's one of them.

214
00:22:22,925 --> 00:22:24,153
<i>Is this really what we wanna do?</i>

215
00:22:24,177 --> 00:22:25,178
He's a traitor.

216
00:22:25,219 --> 00:22:26,471
<i>Kill ourselves off?</i>

217
00:22:26,554 --> 00:22:28,681
<i>Killing is not the answer.</i>

218
00:22:28,806 --> 00:22:30,433
I can't believe he's doing this.

219
00:22:30,558 --> 00:22:32,638
<i>Everyone needs to
lay down their weapons immediately.</i>

220
00:22:32,977 --> 00:22:34,187
Traitor!

221
00:22:34,270 --> 00:22:35,855
He's not one of us!

222
00:22:35,938 --> 00:22:37,482
This is treason!

223
00:22:38,107 --> 00:22:40,360
<i>Are you calling for a ceasefire?</i>

224
00:22:41,235 --> 00:22:43,112
<i>Yeah. I am.</i>

225
00:22:43,154 --> 00:22:44,363
You're a puppet!

226
00:22:44,405 --> 00:22:45,531
Hang him!

227
00:22:45,573 --> 00:22:48,326
<i>I want everyone to stop
the senseless violence.</i>

228
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:50,995
<i>This is not the path to change.</i>

229
00:22:51,037 --> 00:22:52,330
Traitor!

230
00:22:52,371 --> 00:22:55,208
<i>It's not the path to justice.</i>

231
00:23:18,314 --> 00:23:20,316
There can't be a ceasefire.

232
00:23:22,110 --> 00:23:24,237
Not after everything Snow's done.

233
00:23:25,696 --> 00:23:27,740
He could have done a lot of damage tonight.

234
00:23:27,990 --> 00:23:31,494
Most districts, people are still
too afraid to join. They need the courage.

235
00:23:31,619 --> 00:23:33,162
Why do you think he said that?

236
00:23:35,623 --> 00:23:37,458
I don't know. Maybe he was forced.

237
00:23:42,588 --> 00:23:44,549
He didn't look that bad.

238
00:23:46,926 --> 00:23:49,262
Maybe he made some kind of deal
to protect you.

239
00:23:52,431 --> 00:23:54,308
He's still playing the game.

240
00:24:02,984 --> 00:24:05,736
No! No! No!

241
00:24:11,159 --> 00:24:14,245
I'm sorry. It's just a nightmare.

242
00:24:14,287 --> 00:24:16,122
That's okay. I get 'em, too.

243
00:24:20,668 --> 00:24:21,752
Peeta,

244
00:24:24,005 --> 00:24:25,381
will you stay with me?

245
00:24:26,174 --> 00:24:27,425
Yeah.

246
00:24:39,770 --> 00:24:40,813
Always.

247
00:24:48,362 --> 00:24:49,614
Hey.

248
00:24:50,781 --> 00:24:52,325
Can't sleep?

249
00:25:11,219 --> 00:25:12,678
Tell me what's happening.

250
00:25:14,138 --> 00:25:15,765
I'm good at keeping secrets.

251
00:25:16,891 --> 00:25:18,059
Even from Mom.

252
00:25:23,981 --> 00:25:26,359
No one hates the Capitol more than me.

253
00:25:28,778 --> 00:25:32,031
And I wanna help. But I just keep thinking,

254
00:25:33,491 --> 00:25:36,452
even if we win this war,
what happens to Peeta?

255
00:25:38,204 --> 00:25:41,374
I know he's not safe there,
but he's definitely not safe here.

256
00:25:41,832 --> 00:25:44,835
I don't think you know
how important you are to them.

257
00:25:45,836 --> 00:25:49,048
If you want something,
you just have to ask.

258
00:25:50,841 --> 00:25:55,304
You could demand almost anything.
They'd have to agree to it.

259
00:25:56,347 --> 00:25:58,975
I should wake you up
more often, Little Duck.

260
00:26:01,435 --> 00:26:03,020
Get some sleep now.

261
00:26:04,522 --> 00:26:05,731
You, too.

262
00:26:12,655 --> 00:26:14,615
<i>Thank you for agreeing to meet with me.</i>

263
00:26:15,241 --> 00:26:17,576
I've decided I'll be your Mockingjay.

264
00:26:18,119 --> 00:26:21,038
But I have some conditions.

265
00:26:27,336 --> 00:26:31,465
Peeta and the other Tributes,
Johanna Mason and Annie Cresta,

266
00:26:31,757 --> 00:26:34,093
will be rescued at the
earliest opportunity.

267
00:26:34,260 --> 00:26:36,345
If and when Peeta is liberated,

268
00:26:36,554 --> 00:26:39,098
he will receive
a full and unconditional pardon.

269
00:26:39,181 --> 00:26:43,352
No punishment will be inflicted.
And the same goes for the other Tributes.

270
00:26:47,857 --> 00:26:48,941
No.

271
00:26:49,900 --> 00:26:52,361
It's not their fault
you abandoned them in the arena.

272
00:26:52,695 --> 00:26:55,072
They're doing and saying
whatever they can to survive.

273
00:26:55,114 --> 00:26:57,491
Individuals don't make demands in 13.

274
00:26:57,742 --> 00:27:00,870
There will be a tribunal.
And a fair judgment.

275
00:27:01,579 --> 00:27:02,830
Thank you.

276
00:27:04,248 --> 00:27:06,459
The Victors will be granted immunity.

277
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:09,879
And you will announce that
in front of the entire population of 13.

278
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:12,673
You will hold yourself
and your government responsible

279
00:27:12,715 --> 00:27:15,134
or you will find another Mockingjay.

280
00:27:15,176 --> 00:27:17,845
That's it. That's her. Right there.

281
00:27:18,596 --> 00:27:20,264
Isn't that who I promised you?

282
00:27:20,556 --> 00:27:24,852
She wears the costume.
Gunfire in the background. A hint of smoke.

283
00:27:25,269 --> 00:27:26,771
Our Mockingjay.

284
00:27:28,064 --> 00:27:31,651
Madam President, we're losing ground,
because the people are losing heart.

285
00:27:31,817 --> 00:27:34,737
This is worth the risk.
She's worth the risk.

286
00:27:34,862 --> 00:27:37,406
Pardons, tribunals. Power of the people.

287
00:27:37,448 --> 00:27:39,992
It can all be the bedrock
of the new Panem, but,

288
00:27:40,910 --> 00:27:45,623
in wartime I think even the noblest of
causes can be bent a little bit. Right?

289
00:27:50,294 --> 00:27:52,671
Do you have any other conditions?

290
00:27:58,135 --> 00:28:00,096
My sister gets to keep her cat.

291
00:28:15,569 --> 00:28:16,696
Go away.

292
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:23,661
Is it visiting hours again?

293
00:28:25,329 --> 00:28:26,455
Miss Trinket,

294
00:28:28,165 --> 00:28:29,667
you see this door.

295
00:28:30,376 --> 00:28:32,878
It opens. From the inside.

296
00:28:33,379 --> 00:28:36,549
I've told you, these are the standard
living quarters. Same as everyone.

297
00:28:37,007 --> 00:28:39,719
You're not a prisoner.
You're free to join the rest of 13.

298
00:28:41,470 --> 00:28:45,224
Not looking like this. Thank you very much.

299
00:28:45,266 --> 00:28:47,810
We have a bigger issue
than wardrobe, Miss Trinket.

300
00:28:48,352 --> 00:28:50,104
Katniss has agreed to be The Mockingjay.

301
00:28:50,563 --> 00:28:51,730
That poor thing.

302
00:28:51,772 --> 00:28:54,233
And your Girl on Fire is burnt out.

303
00:28:54,442 --> 00:28:56,527
I need you to join this team now.

304
00:28:57,319 --> 00:28:58,863
I need someone she trusts.

305
00:28:59,029 --> 00:29:00,448
What about Haymitch?

306
00:29:00,865 --> 00:29:03,576
He's drying out in some
facility a mile down.

307
00:29:03,701 --> 00:29:07,329
Aiding rebels is not really my forte.

308
00:29:07,371 --> 00:29:11,792
Miss Trinket,
your days in the Capitol are over,

309
00:29:12,084 --> 00:29:13,669
no matter what happens here.

310
00:29:14,879 --> 00:29:17,673
If you wanna play a prisoner of war, fine.

311
00:29:17,923 --> 00:29:19,550
Stay here and rot.

312
00:29:19,717 --> 00:29:21,969
I'll find someone else
to be The Mockingjay's escort.

313
00:29:23,220 --> 00:29:24,263
Who?

314
00:29:27,725 --> 00:29:30,936
Anyone can be replaced.

315
00:29:32,229 --> 00:29:33,856
Not your Mockingjay.

316
00:29:36,108 --> 00:29:39,778
There isn't a soul in this dungeon
who knows the first thing about Katniss.

317
00:29:42,239 --> 00:29:46,994
You honestly believe one of these
cave dwellers is going to take my place?

318
00:29:47,912 --> 00:29:49,163
No.

319
00:30:05,304 --> 00:30:06,764
Good afternoon.

320
00:30:07,348 --> 00:30:09,767
Thank you for interrupting your schedules.

321
00:30:10,601 --> 00:30:13,979
<i>They have already been adjusted
to compensate for the delay.</i>

322
00:30:14,021 --> 00:30:15,648
I hardly ever see children around here.

323
00:30:15,689 --> 00:30:17,876
<i>Please, check in with your unit supervisors
when you resume work.</i>

324
00:30:17,900 --> 00:30:20,653
A lot of them were lost in an epidemic
a few years ago.

325
00:30:20,736 --> 00:30:22,088
<i>I have an announcement
for the citizens of 13.</i>

326
00:30:22,112 --> 00:30:23,572
Coin lost her family, too.

327
00:30:23,989 --> 00:30:25,574
Daughter and a husband.

328
00:30:25,783 --> 00:30:27,993
<i>And our welcome guests from 12.</i>

329
00:30:28,410 --> 00:30:32,331
Katniss Everdeen has consented to be
the face of our cause

330
00:30:32,998 --> 00:30:36,168
to help unite the districts
against the Capitol.

331
00:30:37,002 --> 00:30:42,174
In exchange,
I have promised several concessions.

332
00:30:43,133 --> 00:30:47,680
First, we'll assess all opportunities
for the extraction of the Victors

333
00:30:48,264 --> 00:30:50,432
held hostage in the Capitol.

334
00:30:51,475 --> 00:30:52,726
Peeta Mellark,

335
00:30:56,021 --> 00:30:57,523
Johanna Mason...

336
00:30:58,148 --> 00:30:59,584
Finnick, I made the deal for Annie, too.

337
00:30:59,608 --> 00:31:01,527
And Annie Cresta.

338
00:31:02,653 --> 00:31:06,991
Once freed, they will be granted
full pardon for any and all crimes

339
00:31:07,032 --> 00:31:09,368
committed against the rebel cause.

340
00:31:10,995 --> 00:31:12,079
Good.

341
00:31:12,663 --> 00:31:14,540
That's good, Katniss.

342
00:31:16,625 --> 00:31:20,588
If Katniss Everdeen
fails to fulfill her duties

343
00:31:20,838 --> 00:31:22,548
the deal will be off.

344
00:31:22,840 --> 00:31:27,386
Thank you for your attention.
Please, resume your daily schedules.

345
00:31:31,181 --> 00:31:32,224
Madam President.

346
00:31:32,266 --> 00:31:33,559
Effie Trinket.

347
00:31:33,851 --> 00:31:35,144
Welcome to 13.

348
00:31:35,477 --> 00:31:38,480
Madam President, may I say you are so very

349
00:31:39,356 --> 00:31:40,900
concise.

350
00:31:41,525 --> 00:31:43,235
You believe that there's more to be said?

351
00:31:43,861 --> 00:31:44,903
May I speak freely?

352
00:31:44,945 --> 00:31:46,822
You don't appear to do anything else.

353
00:31:47,489 --> 00:31:50,159
I'm only talking about salesmanship.

354
00:31:50,868 --> 00:31:54,246
The thing with revolutions,
they're a tender flame.

355
00:31:54,288 --> 00:31:58,584
They need to be nurtured
with a little kindling and warmth.

356
00:31:59,043 --> 00:32:00,252
Bit of oxygen.

357
00:32:00,336 --> 00:32:01,670
Oxygen.

358
00:32:02,212 --> 00:32:04,590
One sure way to put
it out is to smother it.

359
00:32:04,882 --> 00:32:07,343
Or to use up all the air in the room.

360
00:32:07,676 --> 00:32:08,969
Excuse me.

361
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:15,309
You know what could use a revolution?
That hair.

362
00:32:16,769 --> 00:32:17,811
Effie?

363
00:32:23,776 --> 00:32:25,152
What are you doing here?

364
00:32:25,235 --> 00:32:26,946
I'm a political refugee.

365
00:32:27,446 --> 00:32:28,781
Plutarch rescued you?

366
00:32:28,864 --> 00:32:31,033
Rescued, yes, that's what he calls it.

367
00:32:31,742 --> 00:32:34,244
You and I were both in the dark.

368
00:32:34,578 --> 00:32:36,997
Now I'm condemned to
this life of jumpsuits.

369
00:32:38,082 --> 00:32:40,459
It is wonderful to see you again.

370
00:32:43,629 --> 00:32:45,005
Can you believe this place?

371
00:32:46,256 --> 00:32:47,883
I miss coffee.

372
00:32:49,259 --> 00:32:51,512
I never knew anyplace could be so strict.

373
00:32:52,012 --> 00:32:56,308
I mean, I thought at least in
the higher ranks there'd be some

374
00:32:57,434 --> 00:32:58,978
side action.

375
00:32:59,395 --> 00:33:01,021
I miss my wigs.

376
00:33:01,271 --> 00:33:04,775
Luckily, I remembered that
this was all the rage when I was coming up.

377
00:33:05,067 --> 00:33:08,153
You know,
everything old can be made new again.

378
00:33:09,279 --> 00:33:10,739
Like democracy.

379
00:33:12,616 --> 00:33:14,451
Which brings me to this.

380
00:33:23,711 --> 00:33:24,837
Cinna.

381
00:33:27,548 --> 00:33:29,049
He's dead, isn't he?

382
00:33:32,636 --> 00:33:34,013
Yes, dear.

383
00:33:37,933 --> 00:33:40,644
He made Plutarch promise
not to show you this

384
00:33:40,769 --> 00:33:43,689
until you'd decided to be The Mockingjay
on your own.

385
00:33:45,232 --> 00:33:48,360
He knew the risks. As we all do.

386
00:33:51,405 --> 00:33:53,407
He believed in this revolution.

387
00:33:55,242 --> 00:33:56,660
He believed in you.

388
00:33:56,910 --> 00:33:58,454
They're beautiful.

389
00:34:00,914 --> 00:34:02,374
They have it.

390
00:34:02,958 --> 00:34:05,002
They have the Mockingjay outfit.

391
00:34:07,129 --> 00:34:11,341
There's not much of a prep team here in 13
but we will make you

392
00:34:12,801 --> 00:34:15,471
the best-dressed rebel in history.

393
00:34:19,641 --> 00:34:20,893
Okay.

394
00:34:22,186 --> 00:34:23,395
Bring up the lights.

395
00:34:41,663 --> 00:34:43,248
Cinna's final touch.

396
00:34:47,669 --> 00:34:51,006
Everyone's either gonna wanna
kiss you, kill you,

397
00:34:51,048 --> 00:34:52,591
or be you.

398
00:34:53,425 --> 00:34:54,718
<i>Perfect.</i>

399
00:34:55,552 --> 00:34:56,929
<i>Absolutely perfect.</i>

400
00:34:57,221 --> 00:34:59,681
Okay. Let's bring up the setting.

401
00:35:07,189 --> 00:35:08,440
<i>Little wind.</i>

402
00:35:09,483 --> 00:35:12,486
<i>Okay, Katniss, we're gonna start you
down on one knee.</i>

403
00:35:12,528 --> 00:35:14,446
- Okay.
<i>- And as you rise up,</i>

404
00:35:14,571 --> 00:35:17,616
<i>you're gonna hold your flag in the air
and deliver your line.</i>

405
00:35:18,075 --> 00:35:21,787
<i>And remember you've just stormed
the outskirts of the Capitol</i>

406
00:35:21,912 --> 00:35:23,592
<i>arm-in-arm with your brothers and sisters.</i>

407
00:35:24,039 --> 00:35:25,082
Okay.

408
00:35:26,250 --> 00:35:28,627
<i>Whenever you're ready.</i>

409
00:35:31,797 --> 00:35:35,175
People of Panem, we fight, we dare, we...

410
00:35:37,886 --> 00:35:38,929
<i>Does she know the line?</i>

411
00:35:38,971 --> 00:35:40,764
I know it. I got it. I'm sorry.

412
00:35:40,806 --> 00:35:42,366
<i>- Let's do it again.</i>
- She's warming up.

413
00:35:42,558 --> 00:35:45,352
<i>All right. With energy. Go.</i>

414
00:35:46,144 --> 00:35:47,896
People of Panem, we fight!

415
00:35:47,938 --> 00:35:51,817
We dare to end this hunger for justice!

416
00:35:52,276 --> 00:35:54,069
<i>You've just been in battle!</i>

417
00:35:54,570 --> 00:35:57,447
<i>I'm sorry. Excuse my outburst.</i>

418
00:35:57,489 --> 00:36:00,075
<i>You've just been in battle.</i>

419
00:36:00,826 --> 00:36:01,994
Let's try it again.

420
00:36:02,369 --> 00:36:03,537
Whenever you're ready.

421
00:36:04,705 --> 00:36:06,874
People of Panem, we fight!

422
00:36:06,915 --> 00:36:11,628
We dare to end this hunger for justice.

423
00:36:22,598 --> 00:36:26,560
And that, my friends,
is how a revolution dies.

424
00:36:30,188 --> 00:36:31,732
Hello, Katniss.

425
00:36:35,319 --> 00:36:36,945
This how you greet an old friend?

426
00:36:38,447 --> 00:36:40,699
Maybe I don't recognize you sober.

427
00:36:42,075 --> 00:36:44,703
I guess it looks as bad as it feels.

428
00:36:46,830 --> 00:36:49,541
<i>People of Panem, we fight!</i>

429
00:36:49,625 --> 00:36:53,378
<i>We dare! We end this hunger for justice!</i>

430
00:37:04,181 --> 00:37:08,977
Madam President, indulge me for a moment,
if you would.

431
00:37:09,061 --> 00:37:11,563
Let's everybody think of one incident

432
00:37:11,647 --> 00:37:14,650
where Katniss Everdeen
genuinely moved you.

433
00:37:14,983 --> 00:37:19,947
Not where you were jealous of her hairstyle
or her dress went up in flames

434
00:37:20,072 --> 00:37:23,116
or she made a halfway decent shot
with an arrow.

435
00:37:23,200 --> 00:37:25,827
And not where Peeta made you like her.

436
00:37:26,912 --> 00:37:29,498
No, I'd like you all to think of one moment

437
00:37:29,539 --> 00:37:32,000
where she made you feel something real.

438
00:37:34,503 --> 00:37:37,547
When she volunteered
for her sister at the Reaping.

439
00:37:38,173 --> 00:37:40,092
Excellent example.

440
00:37:40,801 --> 00:37:41,927
Okay.

441
00:37:42,552 --> 00:37:44,471
I hope that wasn't important.

442
00:37:45,555 --> 00:37:49,643
Okay. "Volunteer for sister."

443
00:37:49,685 --> 00:37:51,520
Good. What else?

444
00:37:51,561 --> 00:37:54,273
When she sang that song for little Rue.

445
00:37:55,065 --> 00:37:57,818
Oh, yeah. Who didn't get choked up at that?

446
00:37:58,318 --> 00:38:01,113
You know, I like you better, Effie,
without all that makeup.

447
00:38:01,238 --> 00:38:03,031
Well, I like you better sober.

448
00:38:04,282 --> 00:38:06,451
When she chose Rue as an ally, as well.

449
00:38:06,576 --> 00:38:07,786
Yes.

450
00:38:08,412 --> 00:38:10,872
Now, what do all these have in common?

451
00:38:11,164 --> 00:38:12,666
No one told her what to do.

452
00:38:13,375 --> 00:38:14,835
Unscripted, yes.

453
00:38:15,752 --> 00:38:17,230
So maybe we should just leave her alone.

454
00:38:17,254 --> 00:38:18,547
And wash her face.

455
00:38:19,381 --> 00:38:21,466
She's still a girl. You made her look 35.

456
00:38:22,551 --> 00:38:26,596
The opportunities for spontaneity
are obviously lacking below ground.

457
00:38:26,930 --> 00:38:31,018
So what you're suggesting
is we toss her into combat?

458
00:38:31,643 --> 00:38:35,897
I can't sanction putting an untrained
civilian in battle just for effect.

459
00:38:35,981 --> 00:38:37,524
This is not the Capitol.

460
00:38:37,607 --> 00:38:40,485
That is exactly what I'm suggesting.
Put her in the field.

461
00:38:40,527 --> 00:38:41,737
No, we can't protect her.

462
00:38:41,778 --> 00:38:45,407
It has to come from her.
That's what people respond to.

463
00:38:45,449 --> 00:38:48,160
You want a symbol for the revolution?

464
00:38:48,201 --> 00:38:50,579
She cannot be coached into it.
Trust me, I know.

465
00:38:50,787 --> 00:38:52,956
Maybe there's someplace
that's less dangerous.

466
00:38:52,998 --> 00:38:55,417
District 8.
They reported heavy bombing last week.

467
00:38:55,584 --> 00:38:56,978
There are no military targets left.

468
00:38:57,002 --> 00:38:58,253
We can't guarantee her safety.

469
00:38:58,295 --> 00:39:00,255
You'll never be able
to guarantee my safety.

470
00:39:01,715 --> 00:39:02,924
I wanna go.

471
00:39:03,175 --> 00:39:04,593
And if you're killed?

472
00:39:06,136 --> 00:39:07,846
Make sure you get it on camera.

473
00:39:11,808 --> 00:39:13,935
I've made you some surprises.

474
00:39:20,067 --> 00:39:21,693
Maybe you wanna try one out.

475
00:39:23,445 --> 00:39:25,006
If you're gonna be
a part of Katniss' propo team,

476
00:39:25,030 --> 00:39:26,698
you may as well look the part.

477
00:39:40,921 --> 00:39:44,591
And this one is for you.

478
00:39:47,302 --> 00:39:50,222
Plutarch wanted you to have a weapon
for the sake of the propos

479
00:39:50,263 --> 00:39:53,767
but I couldn't just make you
a fashion accessory.

480
00:39:56,728 --> 00:39:58,188
It's beautiful.

481
00:40:00,565 --> 00:40:02,275
And look here.

482
00:40:07,614 --> 00:40:10,992
Regular. Incendiary. Explosive arrows.

483
00:40:11,201 --> 00:40:12,452
All color-coded.

484
00:40:13,203 --> 00:40:18,250
And tell Finnick I've got a trident for him

485
00:40:18,750 --> 00:40:20,001
when he's ready.

486
00:40:20,919 --> 00:40:23,547
Might just cheer him up.

487
00:40:25,799 --> 00:40:29,469
Let's not fire the red ones in here.

488
00:40:47,279 --> 00:40:50,949
You had all of this and you just
left the districts to fend for themselves?

489
00:40:52,576 --> 00:40:55,454
It's not that simple, Katniss.
We barely survived.

490
00:40:55,996 --> 00:40:58,582
We weren't in any kind of shape
to launch a counterattack.

491
00:40:59,374 --> 00:41:00,601
Yeah, we could've bombed the Capitol

492
00:41:00,625 --> 00:41:03,105
but they would've retaliated
with at least twice the firepower.

493
00:41:03,253 --> 00:41:04,421
Then what?

494
00:41:05,922 --> 00:41:08,300
There would've been nobody left
to claim victory.

495
00:41:08,758 --> 00:41:12,304
Sounds like exactly what Peeta said
and then you all called him a traitor.

496
00:41:15,390 --> 00:41:16,933
This way, soldier.

497
00:41:18,351 --> 00:41:20,562
You are camera-ready.

498
00:41:22,939 --> 00:41:24,983
Doesn't your comrade look handsome?

499
00:41:27,944 --> 00:41:29,070
Let's go.

500
00:41:31,740 --> 00:41:32,991
Come back safe.

501
00:41:34,993 --> 00:41:36,995
Quick introductions, Katniss.

502
00:41:37,496 --> 00:41:39,915
These people have come a long way
to support the cause.

503
00:41:39,956 --> 00:41:40,999
This is Cressida.

504
00:41:41,041 --> 00:41:44,336
In my opinion one of the best
up-and-coming directors in the Capitol.

505
00:41:44,377 --> 00:41:46,713
Until I up and left. Hey.

506
00:41:47,005 --> 00:41:48,089
Hey.

507
00:41:48,215 --> 00:41:50,383
Let's see what you can do.
All right. Be careful.

508
00:41:52,010 --> 00:41:53,803
This is my assistant, Messalla.

509
00:41:54,137 --> 00:41:55,597
It's an honor to meet you.

510
00:41:55,639 --> 00:41:57,724
And your cameramen over there, Castor.

511
00:41:57,766 --> 00:41:58,808
Hello.

512
00:41:58,934 --> 00:42:00,018
And Pollux.

513
00:42:02,938 --> 00:42:04,356
Let's get locked in.

514
00:42:11,446 --> 00:42:12,781
You're all from the Capitol?

515
00:42:12,822 --> 00:42:14,074
Plutarch got you out?

516
00:42:14,115 --> 00:42:16,076
Don't expect much chitchat from him.

517
00:42:16,284 --> 00:42:19,454
He's an Avox.
Capitol cut his tongue out years ago.

518
00:42:20,080 --> 00:42:24,584
And, no, it wasn't any sort of rescue,
if that's what you mean.

519
00:42:25,835 --> 00:42:27,796
We all fled on our own.

520
00:42:28,088 --> 00:42:29,381
For this.

521
00:42:30,006 --> 00:42:31,049
For you.

522
00:43:02,872 --> 00:43:04,916
This has gotta be fast. In and out.

523
00:43:23,143 --> 00:43:24,394
Move out.

524
00:43:36,364 --> 00:43:38,533
You're alive then. We weren't sure.

525
00:43:38,575 --> 00:43:40,619
Katniss, Commander Paylor, District 8.

526
00:43:40,702 --> 00:43:42,471
Katniss has been recovering,
but she insisted on coming out

527
00:43:42,495 --> 00:43:43,681
and seein' some of your wounded.

528
00:43:43,705 --> 00:43:45,123
Well, we've got plenty of those.

529
00:43:55,508 --> 00:43:58,094
We have a mass grave
a few blocks west, but,

530
00:43:58,136 --> 00:44:00,472
I can't spare the manpower
to move them yet.

531
00:44:01,097 --> 00:44:03,058
Hospital's past that curtain.

532
00:44:03,141 --> 00:44:05,310
Any hope you can give them, it's worth it.

533
00:44:05,560 --> 00:44:08,521
The Capitol's done everything they can
to break us.

534
00:44:08,980 --> 00:44:11,334
Aren't you worried about
having all your wounded in one place?

535
00:44:11,358 --> 00:44:13,158
I think it's better than
leaving them to die.

536
00:44:13,943 --> 00:44:15,153
That's not what I meant.

537
00:44:15,236 --> 00:44:17,322
Well, that's my only other option.

538
00:44:17,739 --> 00:44:20,158
You can come up with another, I'm all ears.

539
00:44:20,950 --> 00:44:22,410
It's right through here.

540
00:44:35,006 --> 00:44:38,134
Don't film me in there. I can't help them.

541
00:44:39,594 --> 00:44:41,513
Just let them see your face.

542
00:44:58,071 --> 00:44:59,114
Excuse me.

543
00:45:05,412 --> 00:45:06,913
Yeah. You all right?

544
00:45:08,623 --> 00:45:10,166
It's okay. Here, it's okay.

545
00:45:10,208 --> 00:45:12,043
I've got you. It's all right.

546
00:45:42,532 --> 00:45:44,117
Katniss Everdeen?

547
00:45:48,413 --> 00:45:50,039
What are you doing here?

548
00:45:51,666 --> 00:45:53,543
I came to see you.

549
00:45:55,545 --> 00:45:57,255
What about the baby?

550
00:46:02,886 --> 00:46:04,095
I lost it.

551
00:46:04,429 --> 00:46:05,847
Are you fighting, Katniss?

552
00:46:08,808 --> 00:46:10,268
You here to fight with us?

553
00:46:11,603 --> 00:46:12,937
I am.

554
00:46:14,606 --> 00:46:15,940
I will.

555
00:46:36,085 --> 00:46:37,212
Tighter.

556
00:46:38,046 --> 00:46:39,297
Tighter, tighter.

557
00:46:47,931 --> 00:46:51,851
Sir, some cameras were damaged
in the bombings,

558
00:46:51,893 --> 00:46:55,146
but we confirmed it's her.

559
00:46:58,608 --> 00:46:59,818
Zoom in.

560
00:47:06,783 --> 00:47:11,496
She was visiting a makeshift hospital.
We're not sure if she's still there.

561
00:47:15,124 --> 00:47:17,627
We can scramble hovercraft
from the border of 11.

562
00:47:17,752 --> 00:47:19,629
We may be able to target her.

563
00:47:22,131 --> 00:47:23,466
Kill the wounded.

564
00:47:23,633 --> 00:47:25,009
Sir...

565
00:47:26,427 --> 00:47:28,805
You wrote that speech yourself, Egeria.

566
00:47:29,973 --> 00:47:34,936
Any association with the Mockingjay symbol
is forbidden.

567
00:47:36,187 --> 00:47:39,732
Everyone inside that hospital
has committed treason.

568
00:47:41,860 --> 00:47:46,364
Show them what it costs
to be friends with Katniss Everdeen.

569
00:47:46,823 --> 00:47:49,143
Your mom's gonna be proud of you
when she sees the footage.

570
00:47:49,826 --> 00:47:51,202
Will this play in the districts?

571
00:47:51,369 --> 00:47:53,496
It'll be tattooed on their eyes.

572
00:47:54,372 --> 00:47:55,873
There's a problem.

573
00:47:56,332 --> 00:47:57,375
What kinda problem?

574
00:47:58,001 --> 00:47:59,711
Incoming bombers from the north.

575
00:48:00,295 --> 00:48:01,588
We need to find cover now.

576
00:48:01,629 --> 00:48:02,880
There's a bunker in there.

577
00:48:16,686 --> 00:48:18,354
Straight ahead and down the stairs.

578
00:48:20,189 --> 00:48:21,232
Katniss!

579
00:48:21,858 --> 00:48:23,067
Katniss!

580
00:48:24,527 --> 00:48:27,739
Everdeen! Everdeen!

581
00:48:28,573 --> 00:48:30,241
Gale, back away from the wall!

582
00:48:46,174 --> 00:48:47,383
You okay?

583
00:48:54,057 --> 00:48:55,224
Move!

584
00:49:02,649 --> 00:49:04,369
They're going after something to the south.

585
00:49:04,484 --> 00:49:05,735
That's towards the hospital.

586
00:49:10,365 --> 00:49:12,659
They're circling back around. Come on!

587
00:49:51,656 --> 00:49:54,575
That's the hospital.
They're targeting the hospital.

588
00:50:49,338 --> 00:50:53,092
Help them! Help them! Get them out!

589
00:50:55,678 --> 00:50:57,054
Katniss?

590
00:50:57,847 --> 00:51:00,683
Katniss, can you tell everyone
what you're seeing right now?

591
00:51:04,020 --> 00:51:05,938
Katniss, what do you wanna say?

592
00:51:16,574 --> 00:51:18,826
I want the rebels to know that I'm alive.

593
00:51:20,036 --> 00:51:21,913
That I'm in District 8

594
00:51:22,121 --> 00:51:24,957
where the Capitol just bombed a hospital

595
00:51:25,291 --> 00:51:29,587
filled with unarmed men,
women and children.

596
00:51:30,379 --> 00:51:32,131
And there will be no survivors.

597
00:51:34,383 --> 00:51:39,263
If you think for one second
that the Capitol will ever treat us fairly

598
00:51:39,430 --> 00:51:41,307
you are lying to yourselves.

599
00:51:41,933 --> 00:51:45,019
Because we know who they are
and what they do.

600
00:51:45,061 --> 00:51:49,315
This is what they do!
And we must fight back.

601
00:51:54,570 --> 00:51:56,948
I have a message for President Snow.

602
00:51:57,657 --> 00:52:00,243
You can torture us and bomb us

603
00:52:00,368 --> 00:52:02,620
and burn our districts to the ground.

604
00:52:03,955 --> 00:52:05,665
But do you see that?

605
00:52:07,083 --> 00:52:08,584
Fire is catching.

606
00:52:09,836 --> 00:52:13,840
And if we burn, you burn with us!

607
00:52:34,819 --> 00:52:37,655
<i>We know who they are and what they do.</i>

608
00:52:37,697 --> 00:52:40,366
<i>This is what they do!</i>

609
00:52:40,575 --> 00:52:42,201
<i>And we must fight back.</i>

610
00:52:43,703 --> 00:52:47,206
<i>You can torture us and bomb us</i>

611
00:52:47,540 --> 00:52:49,834
<i>and burn our districts to the ground.</i>

612
00:52:49,959 --> 00:52:52,003
Plutarch's faith in you wasn't misplaced.

613
00:52:52,044 --> 00:52:53,129
<i>But do you see that?</i>

614
00:52:53,296 --> 00:52:54,380
Thank you.

615
00:52:54,547 --> 00:52:55,798
<i>Fire is catching.</i>

616
00:52:55,840 --> 00:52:57,383
Come up with me for the beginning.

617
00:52:57,592 --> 00:53:01,053
<i>And if we burn, you burn with us!</i>

618
00:53:29,248 --> 00:53:32,460
There is no progress without compromise.

619
00:53:33,461 --> 00:53:36,214
No victory without sacrifice.

620
00:53:37,298 --> 00:53:40,301
But I stand here with The Mockingjay

621
00:53:40,676 --> 00:53:44,138
to announce that our moment has arrived.

622
00:54:10,164 --> 00:54:13,918
Beetee has increased
our use of the airwaves tenfold.

623
00:54:15,169 --> 00:54:19,257
We will broadcast this message
to all the districts tonight.

624
00:54:19,340 --> 00:54:25,096
The Mockingjay's words inspiring everyone
to join the rebellion.

625
00:54:25,304 --> 00:54:28,891
Together, we will become

626
00:54:28,975 --> 00:54:30,935
an alliance to be reckoned with.

627
00:54:33,145 --> 00:54:37,483
Hoorah! Hoorah! Hoorah!

628
00:54:40,569 --> 00:54:43,114
You don't like hearing
a fight song at a funeral?

629
00:54:45,408 --> 00:54:48,619
The more people on our side,
the closer we are to Peeta and Annie.

630
00:54:51,789 --> 00:54:53,124
Yeah.

631
00:55:13,060 --> 00:55:15,229
<i>By order of President Snow</i>

632
00:55:15,313 --> 00:55:18,190
<i>daily production quotas
have been increased.</i>

633
00:55:18,649 --> 00:55:22,486
<i>All work shifts will be extended
by an extra two hours.</i>

634
00:55:22,945 --> 00:55:25,906
<i>Failure to meet these quotas
will not be tolerated.</i>

635
00:55:27,074 --> 00:55:29,285
<i>By order of President Snow</i>

636
00:55:29,326 --> 00:55:32,330
<i>daily production quotas
have been increased.</i>

637
00:56:17,875 --> 00:56:21,045
If we burn, you burn with us!

638
00:56:24,298 --> 00:56:25,716
Yeah!

639
00:56:27,718 --> 00:56:29,136
Yeah!

640
00:56:50,116 --> 00:56:52,159
- I got good news.
- What?

641
00:56:52,201 --> 00:56:53,828
Coin agreed to let us hunt above ground.

642
00:57:45,796 --> 00:57:47,882
He's not even afraid of us.

643
00:57:50,259 --> 00:57:52,059
It's 'cause they've never
been hunted before.

644
00:57:54,513 --> 00:57:56,140
It's almost not fair.

645
00:59:08,837 --> 00:59:10,214
They want us back.

646
00:59:25,354 --> 00:59:26,897
They asked us to head for Command.

647
00:59:26,939 --> 00:59:29,024
All right. I gotta drop these off.

648
00:59:34,363 --> 00:59:38,951
<i>She was arguably our favorite Tribute.</i>

649
00:59:39,368 --> 00:59:43,330
<i>And I think that's what
we all find most astonishing,</i>

650
00:59:43,497 --> 00:59:48,252
<i>is that this girl was
adored in the Capitol.</i>

651
00:59:49,169 --> 00:59:50,754
<i>And I think for you, Peeta,</i>

652
00:59:50,963 --> 00:59:53,591
<i>it must be particularly painful.</i>

653
00:59:54,425 --> 00:59:56,844
<i>I wish I could give this
rose to you, Katniss.</i>

654
00:59:56,927 --> 00:59:59,305
He's changed so much already.
What are they doing to him?

655
00:59:59,346 --> 01:00:03,851
<i>A sweet gesture for a girl
who has inspired such violence.</i>

656
01:00:04,518 --> 01:00:06,079
<i>You must love her very much
to be able to forgive her.</i>

657
01:00:06,103 --> 01:00:07,146
He's shaking.

658
01:00:07,187 --> 01:00:08,439
<i>I don't think that I could.</i>

659
01:00:08,731 --> 01:00:11,859
<i>Unless, of course, Peeta,
you think that perhaps she's being</i>

660
01:00:12,109 --> 01:00:17,072
<i>forced into saying things
that she doesn't even understand.</i>

661
01:00:19,116 --> 01:00:21,702
<i>Yeah. That's exactly what I think.</i>

662
01:00:21,744 --> 01:00:23,078
Even his voice is different.

663
01:00:23,120 --> 01:00:25,748
<i>I think they're using her
to whip up the rebels.</i>

664
01:00:26,040 --> 01:00:27,958
<i>I doubt she even knows what's happening.</i>

665
01:00:28,375 --> 01:00:29,918
<i>And what's really at stake.</i>

666
01:00:30,085 --> 01:00:32,880
<i>Now, Peeta, I doubt that the rebels
will ever let her see this.</i>

667
01:00:33,672 --> 01:00:36,133
<i>But if they do, what would you say to her?</i>

668
01:00:36,467 --> 01:00:39,762
<i>To Katniss Everdeen,
the once sweet Katniss Everdeen.</i>

669
01:00:40,971 --> 01:00:43,307
<i>I would tell her to think for herself.</i>

670
01:00:43,641 --> 01:00:45,225
<i>Yes.</i>

671
01:00:48,395 --> 01:00:49,813
<i>Don't be a fool, Katniss.</i>

672
01:00:50,105 --> 01:00:53,233
<i>I know you never wanted the rebellion.</i>

673
01:00:53,525 --> 01:00:55,152
<i>The things that you did in the Games</i>

674
01:00:55,277 --> 01:00:59,031
<i>were never intended to start all of this.</i>

675
01:01:00,157 --> 01:01:02,659
<i>The rebels have made you
into something that you're not.</i>

676
01:01:02,701 --> 01:01:04,703
<i>Something that could destroy all of us.</i>

677
01:01:05,079 --> 01:01:08,374
<i>So if you have any power or any say</i>

678
01:01:08,916 --> 01:01:11,210
<i>in what they do or how they use you,</i>

679
01:01:13,003 --> 01:01:16,382
<i>please, please, urge them to stop this war</i>

680
01:01:16,548 --> 01:01:18,133
<i>before it's too late.</i>

681
01:01:18,634 --> 01:01:19,802
<i>And ask yourself,</i>

682
01:01:20,386 --> 01:01:22,846
<i>can you trust
the people you're working with?</i>

683
01:01:25,182 --> 01:01:27,017
<i>Do you know what they really want?</i>

684
01:01:27,976 --> 01:01:29,186
We need to respond.

685
01:01:29,228 --> 01:01:34,441
<i>Thank you, Peeta Mellark, for these
revelations about the real Mockingjay.</i>

686
01:01:34,525 --> 01:01:36,026
Did you see what he looks like?

687
01:01:36,068 --> 01:01:37,403
I saw a coward.

688
01:01:37,569 --> 01:01:39,297
You don't have any idea
what he's going through.

689
01:01:39,321 --> 01:01:42,658
I don't care.
I would never say what he just said.

690
01:01:42,991 --> 01:01:45,411
Not if they tortured me.
Not with a gun to my head.

691
01:01:45,452 --> 01:01:48,539
That is the same Peeta
that defended you at the whipping post.

692
01:01:48,622 --> 01:01:51,583
No, it's not.
Now he's only defending himself.

693
01:01:53,669 --> 01:01:55,629
Coin's called a meeting.
We need to respond.

694
01:01:55,671 --> 01:01:57,923
When did "we" become you and Coin?

695
01:01:58,298 --> 01:02:00,092
Everyone has a choice.

696
01:02:00,134 --> 01:02:02,386
How can he sit there in the Capitol
and defend the people

697
01:02:02,428 --> 01:02:04,888
who destroyed his home
and murdered his family?

698
01:02:05,681 --> 01:02:07,141
He doesn't know.

699
01:02:08,142 --> 01:02:12,020
How could he?
Nobody's seen what the Capitol did to 12.

700
01:02:13,021 --> 01:02:14,523
I have to show them.

701
01:02:29,830 --> 01:02:33,125
So I wanna start with you
in front of the Justice Building, okay?

702
01:02:37,463 --> 01:02:39,173
Bang. First shot.

703
01:02:51,768 --> 01:02:53,812
Katniss, tell us what happened here.

704
01:02:57,399 --> 01:02:59,276
We were all standin' right here

705
01:03:04,072 --> 01:03:06,700
watchin' the Games
when you fired that arrow.

706
01:03:07,910 --> 01:03:10,350
The screens just went dark.
Nobody had any idea what happened.

707
01:03:13,332 --> 01:03:15,834
Peacekeepers forced us
back into our homes.

708
01:03:16,752 --> 01:03:19,505
For maybe an hour,
the town was just dead quiet.

709
01:03:22,716 --> 01:03:25,469
Little past 9:00,
we heard their trucks pullin' out.

710
01:03:28,180 --> 01:03:30,641
All of them. Every single Peacekeeper.

711
01:03:33,143 --> 01:03:34,937
And I knew what that meant.

712
01:03:39,233 --> 01:03:40,668
Me and a couple of guys from the mines,

713
01:03:40,692 --> 01:03:44,446
we started pulling people from their houses
and tried to get 'em to the fence line

714
01:03:44,488 --> 01:03:46,490
but a lotta people were
scared of the forest.

715
01:03:47,449 --> 01:03:49,284
So they headed up onto the road.

716
01:03:49,701 --> 01:03:51,495
Make a break for it that way.

717
01:04:00,921 --> 01:04:02,798
Stay with Gale.

718
01:04:07,094 --> 01:04:09,846
915 of us made it to the fence.

719
01:04:11,557 --> 01:04:16,645
Then we watched
as bombers circled back towards the road.

720
01:04:21,483 --> 01:04:23,944
They firebombed them as they ran away.

721
01:04:40,711 --> 01:04:43,505
915 outta 10,000.

722
01:04:50,178 --> 01:04:53,056
I should've grabbed people.
I should've dragged 'em with me.

723
01:04:55,350 --> 01:04:56,893
Some of the kids I could've carried.

724
01:04:56,935 --> 01:04:59,438
You saved so many people, Gale.

725
01:05:00,647 --> 01:05:04,568
Without you, there would be no District 12.
Not even the memory of it.

726
01:05:37,476 --> 01:05:39,311
This is where you kissed me.

727
01:05:40,312 --> 01:05:42,147
I didn't think you remembered that.

728
01:05:51,907 --> 01:05:54,159
I'd have to be dead to forget that.

729
01:05:56,912 --> 01:05:58,288
Maybe not even then.

730
01:06:13,011 --> 01:06:14,638
I knew you'd do that.

731
01:06:15,931 --> 01:06:17,683
How? I didn't.

732
01:06:18,684 --> 01:06:20,310
'Cause I'm in pain.

733
01:06:24,022 --> 01:06:26,149
That's the only way
that I can get your attention.

734
01:06:31,279 --> 01:06:34,241
Don't worry, Katniss. It'll pass.

735
01:06:55,220 --> 01:06:56,346
Hey.

736
01:07:06,356 --> 01:07:08,358
Yeah, that's a mockingjay.

737
01:07:23,749 --> 01:07:25,917
Well, now they'll never shut up.

738
01:07:31,339 --> 01:07:32,716
You want me to sing?

739
01:07:43,852 --> 01:07:49,024
<i>Are you, are you comin' to the tree?</i>

740
01:07:49,691 --> 01:07:52,152
<i>Where they strung up a man</i>

741
01:07:52,360 --> 01:07:54,780
<i>They say who murdered three</i>

742
01:07:55,238 --> 01:07:59,826
<i>Strange things did happen here
No stranger would it be</i>

743
01:08:00,368 --> 01:08:05,332
<i>If we met at midnight in the hanging tree</i>

744
01:08:06,041 --> 01:08:11,087
<i>Are you, are you comin' to the tree?</i>

745
01:08:11,421 --> 01:08:16,593
<i>Where a dead man called out
for his love to flee</i>

746
01:08:17,094 --> 01:08:21,932
<i>Strange things did happen here
No stranger would it be</i>

747
01:08:22,307 --> 01:08:27,437
<i>If we met at midnight in the hanging tree</i>

748
01:08:27,979 --> 01:08:33,026
<i>Are you, are you comin' to the tree?</i>

749
01:08:33,318 --> 01:08:38,448
<i>Where I told you to run
so we'd both be free</i>

750
01:08:38,990 --> 01:08:43,745
<i>Strange things did happen here
No stranger would it be</i>

751
01:08:44,162 --> 01:08:49,292
<i>If we met at midnight in the hanging tree</i>

752
01:08:49,709 --> 01:08:53,922
<i>Are you, are you comin' to the tree?</i>

753
01:08:54,506 --> 01:08:57,634
<i>Wear a necklace of hope
side by side with me</i>

754
01:08:57,676 --> 01:08:59,886
That line was originally
"necklace of rope."

755
01:08:59,928 --> 01:09:01,972
I had it changed to "necklace of hope."

756
01:09:02,514 --> 01:09:04,641
Wow. You are a true wordsmith.

757
01:09:05,517 --> 01:09:07,853
Little on the nose, but,
of course, so is war.

758
01:09:07,894 --> 01:09:09,771
Every district's seeing this?

759
01:09:09,813 --> 01:09:11,648
Yes. But not the Capitol.

760
01:09:12,941 --> 01:09:15,986
I designed this
signal defense system for them.

761
01:09:16,027 --> 01:09:17,904
But I can't find my way through it.

762
01:09:18,405 --> 01:09:20,323
Guess I did my job too well.

763
01:09:20,949 --> 01:09:24,244
At the time, I was just thinking of
the science of it all.

764
01:09:25,537 --> 01:09:26,997
We'll get through it.

765
01:09:27,956 --> 01:09:32,752
<i>Are you, are you comin' to the tree?</i>

766
01:09:32,878 --> 01:09:37,382
<i>Where they strung up a man
they say who murdered three</i>

767
01:09:37,632 --> 01:09:42,053
<i>Strange things did happen here
No stranger would it be</i>

768
01:09:42,220 --> 01:09:47,017
<i>If we met at midnight in the hanging tree</i>

769
01:09:47,142 --> 01:09:51,730
<i>Are you, are you comin' to the tree?</i>

770
01:09:52,063 --> 01:09:56,735
<i>Where a dead man called out
for his love to flee</i>

771
01:09:57,027 --> 01:10:01,364
<i>Strange things did happen here
No stranger would it be</i>

772
01:10:01,531 --> 01:10:06,411
<i>If we met at midnight in the hanging tree</i>

773
01:11:57,522 --> 01:12:02,569
Moves and countermoves.

774
01:12:25,633 --> 01:12:28,720
Katniss, you're wanted in Command.

775
01:12:37,103 --> 01:12:41,816
<i>Tonight, we've received reports
of derailed trains,</i>

776
01:12:42,358 --> 01:12:44,319
<i>of granaries on fire,</i>

777
01:12:44,986 --> 01:12:49,616
<i>and of a savage attack
on the hydroelectric dam in District 5.</i>

778
01:12:49,699 --> 01:12:51,201
What have they done to you?

779
01:12:51,576 --> 01:12:56,664
<i>I'm begging for restraint and decency.</i>

780
01:12:56,706 --> 01:12:59,626
We interrupt your
regularly scheduled horse manure

781
01:12:59,667 --> 01:13:01,211
to bring you...

782
01:13:03,713 --> 01:13:06,049
<i>Comin' to the tree?</i>

783
01:13:06,174 --> 01:13:07,425
That's it. That's our footage.

784
01:13:07,467 --> 01:13:08,718
Beetee's in.

785
01:13:08,968 --> 01:13:10,970
<i>They say who murdered three</i>

786
01:13:11,179 --> 01:13:12,347
<i>Katniss?</i>

787
01:13:12,389 --> 01:13:13,932
He sees it. He sees our propo.

788
01:13:14,182 --> 01:13:16,893
<i>No stranger would it be...</i>

789
01:13:17,685 --> 01:13:18,770
<i>Katniss, are you there?</i>

790
01:13:18,978 --> 01:13:20,271
Peeta.

791
01:13:20,688 --> 01:13:22,440
<i>Katniss?</i>

792
01:13:24,734 --> 01:13:27,112
<i>Peeta, please continue.</i>

793
01:13:28,613 --> 01:13:31,574
<i>You were telling us
about these savage attacks.</i>

794
01:13:32,575 --> 01:13:33,618
<i>Yeah.</i>

795
01:13:38,081 --> 01:13:42,585
<i>The attack on the dam was a callous</i>

796
01:13:43,795 --> 01:13:46,965
<i>and inhuman act of destruction...</i>

797
01:13:47,549 --> 01:13:52,178
<i>Where a dead man called out
for his love to flee</i>

798
01:13:54,430 --> 01:13:55,640
<i>Think about it.</i>

799
01:13:56,808 --> 01:14:00,770
<i>How will this end? What will be left?</i>

800
01:14:01,354 --> 01:14:03,064
<i>No one can survive this.</i>

801
01:14:04,524 --> 01:14:05,900
<i>No one is safe now.</i>

802
01:14:06,151 --> 01:14:07,777
<i>Not here in the Capitol.</i>

803
01:14:09,362 --> 01:14:10,822
<i>Not in any of the districts.</i>

804
01:14:15,368 --> 01:14:17,912
<i>They're coming, Katniss.
They're gonna kill everyone.</i>

805
01:14:17,996 --> 01:14:19,873
<i>And in District 13 you'll
be dead by morning.</i>

806
01:14:21,082 --> 01:14:23,293
He's warning us. That was a warning.

807
01:14:23,835 --> 01:14:24,878
Yes, it was.

808
01:14:24,919 --> 01:14:26,397
We have to get him
out before they kill him.

809
01:14:26,421 --> 01:14:28,798
- Is there anything in the air?
- Nothing on Doppler, ma'am.

810
01:14:28,965 --> 01:14:30,901
He was in the mansion.
He could have overheard something.

811
01:14:30,925 --> 01:14:32,135
Possibly.

812
01:14:36,431 --> 01:14:38,099
It's time for an air raid drill.

813
01:14:46,733 --> 01:14:48,651
<i>This is a code red alert.</i>

814
01:14:48,693 --> 01:14:52,572
<i>Please, remain calm
and begin evacuation protocol.</i>

815
01:14:54,949 --> 01:14:56,826
Prim! Prim!

816
01:14:56,868 --> 01:14:59,996
<i>Proceed to your nearest stairwell
and descend to level 40.</i>

817
01:15:00,413 --> 01:15:03,416
<i>Blast doors will be sealed in six minutes.</i>

818
01:15:05,460 --> 01:15:07,545
<i>This is a code red alert.</i>

819
01:15:07,670 --> 01:15:11,382
<i>Please, remain calm
and begin evacuation protocol.</i>

820
01:15:11,674 --> 01:15:14,761
<i>Proceed in an orderly fashion
to your nearest stairwell</i>

821
01:15:14,802 --> 01:15:17,013
<i>and descend to level 40.</i>

822
01:15:17,263 --> 01:15:21,476
Madam President, three Capitol squadrons
just entered our airspace.

823
01:15:22,101 --> 01:15:23,519
How much time do we have?

824
01:15:23,561 --> 01:15:25,271
They're a few seconds from range.

825
01:15:30,568 --> 01:15:31,986
Prepare to scramble the fleet.

826
01:15:32,028 --> 01:15:33,071
Copy that.

827
01:15:33,112 --> 01:15:36,282
Open up short-range air defense.

828
01:15:40,745 --> 01:15:42,705
Arm long-range missiles for counterattack.

829
01:15:42,747 --> 01:15:45,500
<i>Blast doors will be sealed in five minutes.</i>

830
01:15:53,091 --> 01:15:55,051
<i>This is a code red alert.</i>

831
01:15:55,093 --> 01:15:58,846
<i>Please, remain calm
and begin evacuation protocol.</i>

832
01:15:59,180 --> 01:16:02,308
<i>Proceed in an orderly fashion
to your nearest stairwell</i>

833
01:16:02,350 --> 01:16:04,269
<i>and descend to level 40.</i>

834
01:16:04,352 --> 01:16:07,355
<i>Blast doors will close in four minutes.</i>

835
01:16:10,650 --> 01:16:12,735
<i>This is a code red alert.</i>

836
01:16:12,777 --> 01:16:16,531
<i>Please, remain calm
and begin evacuation protocol.</i>

837
01:16:16,573 --> 01:16:19,909
<i>Proceed in an orderly fashion
to your nearest stairwell</i>

838
01:16:20,034 --> 01:16:22,036
<i>and descend to level 40.</i>

839
01:16:22,078 --> 01:16:25,248
<i>Blast doors will close in three minutes.</i>

840
01:16:30,169 --> 01:16:32,171
<i>This is a code red alert.</i>

841
01:16:32,213 --> 01:16:35,425
<i>Proceed in an orderly fashion
to your nearest stairwell</i>

842
01:16:35,466 --> 01:16:37,510
<i>and descend to level 40.</i>

843
01:16:46,477 --> 01:16:49,605
<i>Continue to the Supply Station
and claim one pack</i>

844
01:16:49,647 --> 01:16:51,899
<i>for each member of your compartment.</i>

845
01:16:52,400 --> 01:16:56,321
<i>Please keep all personal items
within your assigned area.</i>

846
01:16:56,654 --> 01:16:59,282
<i>Be courteous to your fellow citizens.</i>

847
01:17:01,409 --> 01:17:03,494
<i>This is a code red alert.</i>

848
01:17:03,578 --> 01:17:06,581
<i>All citizens should be inside the bunker.</i>

849
01:17:07,081 --> 01:17:10,126
<i>- Blast doors will close in two minutes.</i>
- Mom!

850
01:17:13,171 --> 01:17:14,255
Where's Prim?

851
01:17:14,297 --> 01:17:16,007
I thought she went to find you.

852
01:17:16,049 --> 01:17:17,383
She must still be on the stairs.

853
01:17:17,425 --> 01:17:18,968
There's no one on the stairs.

854
01:17:21,763 --> 01:17:23,139
She went back for the cat.

855
01:17:24,098 --> 01:17:26,225
<i>This is a code red alert.</i>

856
01:17:26,309 --> 01:17:28,686
<i>All citizens should be inside the bunker.</i>

857
01:17:28,728 --> 01:17:29,771
Hey, stop! Stop!

858
01:17:29,812 --> 01:17:32,940
<i>Blast doors will close in one minute.</i>

859
01:17:39,364 --> 01:17:42,408
They hit the far edge of
the northwest quadrant. Penetrated 40 feet.

860
01:17:42,450 --> 01:17:45,745
Missed the living quarters.
Only minor damage to corridors 2 and 3.

861
01:17:45,787 --> 01:17:47,080
Is there any radiation?

862
01:17:47,121 --> 01:17:48,164
None detected.

863
01:17:48,206 --> 01:17:50,041
Doppler shows a fourth wave approaching.

864
01:17:51,084 --> 01:17:55,213
<i>- Blast doors will close in 30 seconds.</i>
- Prim!

865
01:17:57,632 --> 01:17:58,675
Prim!

866
01:17:58,716 --> 01:18:00,176
Katniss!

867
01:18:06,015 --> 01:18:07,642
<i>This is a code red alert.</i>

868
01:18:07,684 --> 01:18:08,810
Katniss!

869
01:18:08,851 --> 01:18:11,354
<i>Blast doors will close in 15 seconds.</i>

870
01:18:11,396 --> 01:18:12,772
Get down here!

871
01:18:13,981 --> 01:18:16,109
- Hurry!
<i>- This is a code red alert.</i>

872
01:18:16,150 --> 01:18:19,737
<i>Blast doors will close in 10 seconds.</i>

873
01:18:20,405 --> 01:18:21,447
<i>Nine...</i>

874
01:18:22,573 --> 01:18:23,616
<i>Eight...</i>

875
01:18:24,784 --> 01:18:25,827
<i>Seven...</i>

876
01:18:27,328 --> 01:18:28,371
<i>Six...</i>

877
01:18:29,997 --> 01:18:31,874
<i>- Five...</i>
- Hold the doors!

878
01:18:32,333 --> 01:18:33,501
<i>Four...</i>

879
01:18:34,961 --> 01:18:36,254
<i>Three...</i>

880
01:18:37,505 --> 01:18:39,382
<i>- Two...</i>
- Wait! Hold the doors!

881
01:18:40,007 --> 01:18:41,384
<i>One.</i>

882
01:18:42,844 --> 01:18:45,221
You went back for the cat?
What were you thinking?

883
01:18:45,263 --> 01:18:48,433
I wasn't gonna leave him behind.
I couldn't live with myself.

884
01:18:49,267 --> 01:18:51,436
<i>Blast doors are now sealed.</i>

885
01:18:51,477 --> 01:18:53,020
I know, Prim.

886
01:18:58,151 --> 01:18:59,402
Let's go.

887
01:19:02,530 --> 01:19:04,532
Damage to the aquifer
in the northwest quadrant.

888
01:19:04,574 --> 01:19:06,200
We lost a transport corridor.

889
01:19:06,242 --> 01:19:07,910
There's nothing else in the northwest.

890
01:19:07,952 --> 01:19:11,122
Our surface-to-air launchers
just took a direct hit in sector 3.

891
01:19:11,456 --> 01:19:15,334
Because we revealed ourselves.
They saw us firing there.

892
01:19:18,546 --> 01:19:20,423
Stand down. Don't launch the fleet.

893
01:19:20,465 --> 01:19:25,052
Another 12 Capitol bombers
approaching sector 3 in attack formation.

894
01:19:25,094 --> 01:19:27,388
Hold fire on their approach.

895
01:19:31,601 --> 01:19:32,685
What'd they hit?

896
01:19:32,727 --> 01:19:35,021
Bedrock. But there's
debris in the ventilation shaft.

897
01:19:35,062 --> 01:19:36,564
They're not targeting our fleet.

898
01:19:36,606 --> 01:19:37,857
Or our Special Weaponry.

899
01:19:37,899 --> 01:19:39,859
They don't know what we have
or where we have it.

900
01:19:40,401 --> 01:19:42,463
Can you confirm
that everyone's safely in the bunker?

901
01:19:42,487 --> 01:19:43,613
Already done.

902
01:19:44,405 --> 01:19:47,116
Conceal all remaining anti-aircraft guns.

903
01:19:47,158 --> 01:19:49,786
Seal launching pads
and ventilation corridors.

904
01:19:49,952 --> 01:19:53,289
We are gonna wait this out.
This is what we're built for.

905
01:19:53,456 --> 01:19:55,583
They'll seal us in here like a tomb.

906
01:19:56,000 --> 01:19:57,811
The Capitol's working off
some outdated information.

907
01:19:57,835 --> 01:19:59,195
I'd rather not update it for them.

908
01:19:59,462 --> 01:20:01,631
Madam President, I
know it's not my place...

909
01:20:01,672 --> 01:20:04,552
It's not. You're a welcome guest,
but you're out of your depth down here.

910
01:20:05,134 --> 01:20:07,929
Reduce oxygen to 14 % to conserve it.

911
01:20:07,970 --> 01:20:09,055
Copy that.

912
01:20:10,014 --> 01:20:13,476
Take a deep breath, Mr. Heavensbee.
It's gonna be a long night.

913
01:20:52,306 --> 01:20:54,976
Prim, talk about something. Anything.

914
01:20:58,479 --> 01:21:00,398
They promoted me at the hospital.

915
01:21:01,566 --> 01:21:03,109
I forgot to tell you.

916
01:21:03,150 --> 01:21:04,550
They're training me to be a doctor.

917
01:21:06,821 --> 01:21:08,531
They'd be stupid not to.

918
01:22:23,189 --> 01:22:24,231
Hey.

919
01:22:25,566 --> 01:22:26,609
Can I sit?

920
01:22:26,817 --> 01:22:27,860
Yeah.

921
01:22:32,406 --> 01:22:34,867
Snow's using Annie to punish you.

922
01:22:35,242 --> 01:22:37,328
He's taunting us with them.

923
01:22:38,788 --> 01:22:43,209
I didn't understand until just now
watching that stupid cat.

924
01:22:51,467 --> 01:22:53,719
After your first Games,

925
01:22:54,261 --> 01:22:57,723
I thought the whole romance was an act.

926
01:22:59,684 --> 01:23:02,812
We all expected you
to continue that strategy.

927
01:23:02,979 --> 01:23:08,109
But it wasn't until Peeta's heart stopped
and he nearly died that

928
01:23:10,486 --> 01:23:12,905
I knew I'd misjudged you.

929
01:23:13,614 --> 01:23:14,991
You love him.

930
01:23:17,243 --> 01:23:20,204
I'm not saying in what way.
Maybe you don't even know yourself.

931
01:23:20,371 --> 01:23:23,082
But anyone paying attention can see it.

932
01:23:24,208 --> 01:23:26,085
How do you live with it?

933
01:23:28,295 --> 01:23:32,258
I drag myself outta nightmares
and there's no relief in waking up.

934
01:23:32,925 --> 01:23:37,054
But it's better not to give in to it.

935
01:23:38,973 --> 01:23:41,350
Takes 10 times longer
to put yourself back together

936
01:23:41,517 --> 01:23:43,394
than it does to fall apart.

937
01:23:53,529 --> 01:23:56,741
Katniss? Katniss?

938
01:23:57,533 --> 01:23:58,868
Come with me.

939
01:24:04,498 --> 01:24:07,001
We took their best shot. Didn't we?

940
01:24:08,335 --> 01:24:09,587
Yeah.

941
01:24:10,171 --> 01:24:11,714
Your mother and sister okay?

942
01:24:12,006 --> 01:24:13,340
Yeah, they're fine.

943
01:24:13,507 --> 01:24:15,760
I need you to do something for us.

944
01:24:16,218 --> 01:24:19,972
I need you to tell Panem
that we survived an attack by the Capitol

945
01:24:20,139 --> 01:24:21,974
with no casualties.

946
01:24:22,141 --> 01:24:24,602
And we remain fully operational.

947
01:24:25,478 --> 01:24:26,645
Okay.

948
01:24:27,354 --> 01:24:28,898
You should know something.

949
01:24:29,732 --> 01:24:34,278
We had eight extra minutes of civilian
evacuation because of Peeta's warning.

950
01:24:35,237 --> 01:24:36,947
I won't forget that.

951
01:24:38,157 --> 01:24:39,492
Thank you.

952
01:24:54,799 --> 01:24:59,804
So Katniss,
it's "13 is alive and well and so am I."

953
01:25:01,388 --> 01:25:02,473
Katniss?

954
01:25:04,642 --> 01:25:05,726
Katniss.

955
01:25:07,103 --> 01:25:10,022
Never one to waste it in rehearsal, I know.

956
01:26:15,045 --> 01:26:16,922
Why would they drop these?

957
01:26:20,301 --> 01:26:21,635
For me.

958
01:26:21,927 --> 01:26:23,679
Ready to go, Katniss?

959
01:26:25,097 --> 01:26:27,224
We're gonna do this, just like District 8.

960
01:26:30,519 --> 01:26:32,271
Tell me about the roses.

961
01:26:37,610 --> 01:26:42,156
Tell Snow 13 is alive and well.

962
01:26:46,452 --> 01:26:47,828
He's gonna kill Peeta.

963
01:26:47,870 --> 01:26:50,497
Let's try again. Can you speak up?
We don't have a mic on you.

964
01:26:50,748 --> 01:26:54,543
"13 is alive and well and so am I."

965
01:26:57,880 --> 01:26:59,757
He's gonna kill Peeta.

966
01:27:02,760 --> 01:27:03,802
I can't.

967
01:27:03,886 --> 01:27:05,012
Katniss?

968
01:27:06,722 --> 01:27:08,098
You can do it, Katniss.

969
01:27:08,224 --> 01:27:09,391
I can't do this.

970
01:27:09,433 --> 01:27:12,603
"13 is alive and well and so am I."

971
01:27:12,811 --> 01:27:15,814
He's just gonna keep...
He's never gonna stop.

972
01:27:15,856 --> 01:27:17,209
Cressida, we should cut the cameras.

973
01:27:17,233 --> 01:27:18,418
- As long as I'm The Mockingjay.
- It's okay, Katniss.

974
01:27:18,442 --> 01:27:21,904
No. He warned me. He warned me about this.

975
01:27:23,113 --> 01:27:25,532
He's doing this because I'm The Mockingjay.

976
01:27:26,033 --> 01:27:28,202
He's punishing Peeta to punish me.

977
01:27:28,619 --> 01:27:29,745
No.

978
01:27:31,372 --> 01:27:32,665
No, I can't do this.

979
01:27:32,915 --> 01:27:33,958
Katniss.

980
01:27:33,999 --> 01:27:36,251
Don't make me do this!

981
01:27:36,293 --> 01:27:37,378
Let her go.

982
01:27:37,544 --> 01:27:40,756
I gotta get out of here.

983
01:27:59,942 --> 01:28:02,236
So this is the end?

984
01:28:02,903 --> 01:28:05,614
I s'pose you're just gonna
hide down here forever?

985
01:28:06,448 --> 01:28:08,826
I can't be The Mockingjay.

986
01:28:09,326 --> 01:28:12,454
Not The Mockingjay. Just Katniss.

987
01:28:14,999 --> 01:28:19,545
You know, you're the only real friend
I have down here.

988
01:28:24,091 --> 01:28:28,721
I don't suppose they gave you
any kind of medication?

989
01:28:28,762 --> 01:28:29,930
You're unbelievable.

990
01:28:29,972 --> 01:28:31,974
Okay, but I meant what I said.

991
01:28:33,142 --> 01:28:36,478
Look, the reason I'm
here is to let you know

992
01:28:37,187 --> 01:28:38,689
they're rescuing Peeta.

993
01:28:40,315 --> 01:28:41,442
What?

994
01:28:41,483 --> 01:28:45,154
The dam went down in District 5,
took out most of the power to the Capitol.

995
01:28:45,195 --> 01:28:47,156
Knocked out their signal defense.

996
01:28:47,239 --> 01:28:51,368
Beetee's inside their system now,
wreaking all kinds of havoc.

997
01:28:51,994 --> 01:28:54,580
A window is open to us.
How much longer? I don't know.

998
01:28:54,621 --> 01:28:57,332
I guess until the Capitol
can get the power back on.

999
01:28:57,374 --> 01:28:58,625
And President Coin?

1000
01:28:58,667 --> 01:29:01,754
You know, I can never
fully support that woman

1001
01:29:01,795 --> 01:29:06,842
in light of the prohibition
they have going on around this place,

1002
01:29:06,967 --> 01:29:09,636
but Plutarch got word

1003
01:29:09,678 --> 01:29:12,306
that Peeta and the others
are in the Tribute Center.

1004
01:29:12,431 --> 01:29:15,684
And with the power out,
Coin sees this as an opportunity.

1005
01:29:15,851 --> 01:29:19,897
She knows that Peeta is the Capitol's
weapon. The same way you're ours.

1006
01:29:20,022 --> 01:29:23,567
And as opposed to having you two
pointing at each other,

1007
01:29:23,984 --> 01:29:25,694
she's going to get him.

1008
01:29:26,403 --> 01:29:27,529
I have to go help.

1009
01:29:27,571 --> 01:29:29,656
Hey, whoa, kiddo. Wait.

1010
01:29:29,865 --> 01:29:33,285
Come on. Are you just gonna jump
outta the vent and go storm the Capitol?

1011
01:29:33,327 --> 01:29:35,454
Besides, it's already underway.

1012
01:29:36,246 --> 01:29:39,416
Six soldiers went in. Volunteer only.

1013
01:29:39,583 --> 01:29:43,045
And guess who was
the first brave soul to sign up.

1014
01:29:43,754 --> 01:29:45,130
Gale.

1015
01:29:54,723 --> 01:29:56,558
- Okay, Finnick?
- Yeah.

1016
01:29:56,934 --> 01:30:00,813
Go in the center there. Those rocks.

1017
01:30:04,441 --> 01:30:06,485
Castor, to left.

1018
01:30:06,693 --> 01:30:08,278
Pollux, you're with me.

1019
01:30:08,695 --> 01:30:10,614
So we'll go straight to camera.

1020
01:30:10,864 --> 01:30:13,408
Okay? Finnick?

1021
01:30:13,450 --> 01:30:14,535
Yeah.

1022
01:30:14,868 --> 01:30:16,120
Okay.

1023
01:30:16,620 --> 01:30:20,916
Take your time. Just remember
to keep talking and don't stop.

1024
01:30:24,586 --> 01:30:26,588
This is Finnick Odair.

1025
01:30:27,714 --> 01:30:30,425
<i>Winner of the 65th Hunger Games.</i>

1026
01:30:30,759 --> 01:30:34,138
<i>And I'm coming to you from District 13,
alive and well.</i>

1027
01:30:34,471 --> 01:30:37,266
<i>We've survived an assault from the Capitol.</i>

1028
01:30:37,724 --> 01:30:40,352
<i>But I'm not here to give you recent news.</i>

1029
01:30:40,561 --> 01:30:42,438
Why is Finnick doing a propo?

1030
01:30:42,729 --> 01:30:44,273
It's a lot more than that.

1031
01:30:44,314 --> 01:30:46,275
Beetee's commandeered the system.

1032
01:30:46,400 --> 01:30:48,277
Now that they're down to generator power

1033
01:30:48,318 --> 01:30:50,463
there's a more limited range of frequencies
available to them.

1034
01:30:50,487 --> 01:30:52,364
And I'm filling them all up with Finnick.

1035
01:30:52,489 --> 01:30:55,367
Not many will see it, but whoever does
will think it's another propo.

1036
01:30:55,576 --> 01:30:58,954
What they don't know is this broadcast
is jamming their entire system with noise.

1037
01:30:58,996 --> 01:31:01,748
Early defense warning,
internal communications, everything.

1038
01:31:02,332 --> 01:31:03,810
As long as the broadcast goes through,

1039
01:31:03,834 --> 01:31:06,295
our team should be able
to get in and out undetected.

1040
01:31:06,461 --> 01:31:09,506
<i>The truth.
Not the myths about a life of luxury.</i>

1041
01:31:09,548 --> 01:31:12,718
<i>Not the lie about glory for your homeland.</i>

1042
01:31:12,801 --> 01:31:15,012
<i>You can survive the arena.</i>

1043
01:31:15,262 --> 01:31:17,639
<i>The moment you leave, you're a slave.</i>

1044
01:31:30,903 --> 01:31:35,282
<i>Mockingjay One, you are one minute out
from perimeter defense.</i>

1045
01:31:35,324 --> 01:31:36,492
Going dark.

1046
01:31:36,617 --> 01:31:38,118
<i>Stay low in case they're online.</i>

1047
01:31:39,953 --> 01:31:42,497
<i>President Snow used to sell me.</i>

1048
01:31:42,664 --> 01:31:45,834
<i>Or my body, at least.
I wasn't the only one.</i>

1049
01:31:45,876 --> 01:31:48,337
<i>If a Victor is considered desirable,</i>

1050
01:31:48,378 --> 01:31:51,548
<i>the President gives them as a reward
or allows people to buy them.</i>

1051
01:31:51,632 --> 01:31:54,676
<i>If you refuse, he kills someone you love.</i>

1052
01:31:54,801 --> 01:31:58,055
Mockingjay One, you are 20 seconds
from perimeter defense.

1053
01:32:03,810 --> 01:32:05,020
Ten seconds.

1054
01:32:05,103 --> 01:32:06,980
Nine... Eight...

1055
01:32:07,356 --> 01:32:10,234
<i>Seven... Six... Five...</i>

1056
01:32:10,817 --> 01:32:13,737
<i>Four... Three... Two...</i>

1057
01:32:14,571 --> 01:32:15,739
<i>One.</i>

1058
01:32:23,997 --> 01:32:27,376
<i>No response from perimeter defense.
We're inside Capitol airspace.</i>

1059
01:32:27,417 --> 01:32:29,044
<i>To make themselves feel better,</i>

1060
01:32:29,086 --> 01:32:31,380
<i>my patrons would make presents
of money or jewelry.</i>

1061
01:32:31,922 --> 01:32:36,551
<i>But I found a much more valuable
form of payment.</i>

1062
01:32:36,802 --> 01:32:37,886
<i>Secrets.</i>

1063
01:32:38,011 --> 01:32:39,263
Gear up.

1064
01:32:59,992 --> 01:33:01,243
Switching to Night View.

1065
01:33:09,918 --> 01:33:11,295
There.

1066
01:33:14,131 --> 01:33:16,800
Command, we have visual
on the Tribute Center.

1067
01:33:16,842 --> 01:33:18,844
<i>Initiating final approach.</i>

1068
01:33:23,432 --> 01:33:24,766
Masks on.

1069
01:33:30,063 --> 01:33:33,608
<i>See, I know all the depravity,
the deceit and the cruelty</i>

1070
01:33:33,650 --> 01:33:36,069
<i>of the Capitol's pampered elite.</i>

1071
01:33:37,029 --> 01:33:41,283
<i>But the biggest secrets are about
our good President, Coriolanus Snow.</i>

1072
01:33:49,166 --> 01:33:50,459
Open the door.

1073
01:34:00,135 --> 01:34:01,553
<i>Command, this is Team Leader.</i>

1074
01:34:01,595 --> 01:34:04,765
<i>Prepare to deploy gas.
We will confirm once inside.</i>

1075
01:34:08,477 --> 01:34:11,897
<i>Such a young man when he rose to power.
Such a clever one to keep it.</i>

1076
01:34:11,938 --> 01:34:15,317
<i>How, you may ask, did he do it?</i>

1077
01:34:17,027 --> 01:34:18,278
<i>One word.</i>

1078
01:34:19,279 --> 01:34:20,614
<i>Poison.</i>

1079
01:34:26,995 --> 01:34:28,330
Get ready to drop.

1080
01:34:56,024 --> 01:34:58,693
<i>He stopped every mutiny
before it even started.</i>

1081
01:35:09,830 --> 01:35:10,872
Clear.

1082
01:35:14,626 --> 01:35:18,922
Clear. Command, we're inside.
Heading toward target number one.

1083
01:35:19,047 --> 01:35:21,800
Cell P45 lower level 2C.

1084
01:35:22,843 --> 01:35:23,927
Gas.

1085
01:35:24,344 --> 01:35:27,723
<i>There are so many mysterious deaths
to adversaries.</i>

1086
01:35:29,182 --> 01:35:31,393
<i>Even to allies who were threats.</i>

1087
01:35:42,863 --> 01:35:45,657
<i>Snow would drink from the same cup,
to deflect suspicion.</i>

1088
01:35:45,699 --> 01:35:48,702
<i>But antidotes don't always work,</i>

1089
01:35:48,827 --> 01:35:51,705
<i>which is why he wears roses
that reek of perfume.</i>

1090
01:35:52,038 --> 01:35:56,668
<i>Help cover the scent of blood from sores
in his mouth that will never heal.</i>

1091
01:36:21,526 --> 01:36:22,652
Gale.

1092
01:36:26,823 --> 01:36:29,451
<i>But he can't hide the scent
of who he really is.</i>

1093
01:36:29,493 --> 01:36:31,286
<i>He kills without mercy.</i>

1094
01:36:31,578 --> 01:36:34,164
<i>He rules with deception and fear.</i>

1095
01:36:59,648 --> 01:37:03,318
<i>His weapon of choice is the only thing
suited to such a man.</i>

1096
01:37:03,360 --> 01:37:06,738
<i>Poison. The perfect weapon for a snake.</i>

1097
01:37:09,115 --> 01:37:10,575
<i>What is this place?</i>

1098
01:37:21,461 --> 01:37:22,837
- Beetee?
- I'm losing them.

1099
01:37:23,129 --> 01:37:24,381
Powering back up.

1100
01:37:26,633 --> 01:37:30,262
Ma'am, the Capitol air defense system
is rebooting. It's coming back online.

1101
01:37:30,303 --> 01:37:32,138
Must be diverting power
from another source.

1102
01:37:32,180 --> 01:37:34,867
And filtering transmissions.
Another 60 seconds and we'll be cut off.

1103
01:37:34,891 --> 01:37:37,143
Madam President,
should we call back the hovercraft?

1104
01:37:38,979 --> 01:37:40,355
Broadcast me.

1105
01:37:40,772 --> 01:37:44,067
If Snow's watching this, maybe
he'll let the signal in, if he sees me.

1106
01:37:44,985 --> 01:37:46,736
Put me on the air so he can see me.

1107
01:37:46,778 --> 01:37:47,946
Yes. Yes.

1108
01:37:48,280 --> 01:37:49,364
Put her on.

1109
01:37:49,489 --> 01:37:51,700
Can we do this? Can we still get in?

1110
01:37:51,908 --> 01:37:54,494
Yes. For the moment.
The line's open. He will only see you.

1111
01:37:54,578 --> 01:37:56,121
Okay, Katniss, go.

1112
01:37:56,538 --> 01:37:59,457
President Snow?
President Snow. It's Katniss.

1113
01:37:59,583 --> 01:38:02,210
There's no guarantee he's even watching.

1114
01:38:02,335 --> 01:38:04,045
I know, but he might be.

1115
01:38:04,087 --> 01:38:07,257
President Snow, I need to speak with you.
Are you there?

1116
01:38:08,633 --> 01:38:12,429
President Snow, it's Katniss.
Can you hear me?

1117
01:38:13,722 --> 01:38:15,265
I need to speak with you.

1118
01:38:17,350 --> 01:38:19,477
President Snow, it's Katniss.

1119
01:38:19,519 --> 01:38:22,731
President Snow, are you there?

1120
01:38:25,859 --> 01:38:27,402
Can you hear me?

1121
01:38:33,074 --> 01:38:34,117
President Snow...

1122
01:38:34,200 --> 01:38:36,870
<i>Miss Everdeen. What an honor.</i>

1123
01:38:38,580 --> 01:38:42,709
<i>I don't imagine you're calling
to thank me for the roses.</i>

1124
01:38:44,836 --> 01:38:46,212
I never asked for this.

1125
01:38:47,672 --> 01:38:49,507
I never asked to be in the Games.

1126
01:38:49,758 --> 01:38:52,844
- Boggs? Come in. Boggs?
- I never asked to be The Mockingjay.

1127
01:38:54,471 --> 01:38:58,099
Just wanted to save my sister.
And keep Peeta alive.

1128
01:38:58,642 --> 01:39:00,769
Come in. Boggs?

1129
01:39:01,645 --> 01:39:05,273
Please, just let him go.
And I will stop being The Mockingjay.

1130
01:39:05,315 --> 01:39:07,859
I will disappear.
You will never have to see me ever again.

1131
01:39:07,901 --> 01:39:09,361
<i>Miss Everdeen.</i>

1132
01:39:09,694 --> 01:39:12,280
- Boggs, come in.
<i>- You couldn't run from this...</i>

1133
01:39:12,322 --> 01:39:13,448
<i>Copy.</i>

1134
01:39:13,490 --> 01:39:15,909
<i>Any more than you could have run
from the Games.</i>

1135
01:39:16,868 --> 01:39:18,912
Command, I need a situation report.

1136
01:39:18,995 --> 01:39:21,539
<i>Boggs, we're running out of time. Hurry.</i>

1137
01:39:23,208 --> 01:39:24,334
Let's move.

1138
01:39:24,417 --> 01:39:25,543
<i>Please.</i>

1139
01:39:25,752 --> 01:39:27,295
You've won.

1140
01:39:30,632 --> 01:39:32,133
<i>You've already beaten me.</i>

1141
01:39:35,470 --> 01:39:38,264
Release Peeta. And take me instead.

1142
01:39:40,433 --> 01:39:45,730
<i>We're long past the opportunity
for noble sacrifice.</i>

1143
01:39:45,814 --> 01:39:47,524
Then tell me what to do.

1144
01:39:47,649 --> 01:39:49,776
<i>I've always kept my promises, haven't I?</i>

1145
01:39:49,818 --> 01:39:52,320
<i>You said you didn't want a war.</i>

1146
01:39:52,904 --> 01:39:54,781
<i>And that's just what's happened.</i>

1147
01:39:56,199 --> 01:39:59,327
<i>I told you what a fragile thing peace was.</i>

1148
01:39:59,452 --> 01:40:03,999
<i>And still, like a child,
you took pleasure in breaking it.</i>

1149
01:40:05,417 --> 01:40:07,335
<i>I know what you are.</i>

1150
01:40:07,544 --> 01:40:11,089
<i>I know you can't see past
your narrowest concerns.</i>

1151
01:40:11,297 --> 01:40:13,341
<i>But please, Miss Everdeen.</i>

1152
01:40:14,384 --> 01:40:17,053
<i>I doubt you know what honesty is anymore.</i>

1153
01:40:17,262 --> 01:40:18,805
Command, we're at the first target.

1154
01:40:18,888 --> 01:40:21,975
Preparing to extract Peeta.
Will confirm when he's in hand.

1155
01:40:24,853 --> 01:40:27,105
Mockingjay One,
prepare hovercraft for evac.

1156
01:40:27,147 --> 01:40:30,108
You asked me to convince you
that I was in love with Peeta.

1157
01:40:30,233 --> 01:40:32,152
Haven't I at least done that?

1158
01:40:33,194 --> 01:40:34,821
<i>Miss Everdeen,</i>

1159
01:40:36,698 --> 01:40:39,701
<i>it's the things we love most</i>

1160
01:40:40,618 --> 01:40:42,203
<i>that destroy us.</i>

1161
01:40:44,122 --> 01:40:48,126
<i>I want you to remember that I said that.</i>

1162
01:40:53,798 --> 01:40:56,885
<i>Don't you think I know your friends
are in the Tribute Center?</i>

1163
01:40:59,679 --> 01:41:00,805
<i>Cut them off.</i>

1164
01:41:02,182 --> 01:41:03,892
- What happened?
- Boggs, come in.

1165
01:41:03,933 --> 01:41:05,059
What happened?

1166
01:41:05,101 --> 01:41:06,728
Boggs, come in. Do you read me?

1167
01:41:07,520 --> 01:41:10,120
- He knows that they're in there. It's a trap.
- Katniss, hold it.

1168
01:41:10,482 --> 01:41:13,252
We have to get a hold of them.
We have to tell them to get out. He knows.

1169
01:41:13,276 --> 01:41:15,320
There's no signal. We can't contact them.

1170
01:41:15,653 --> 01:41:19,240
No. Haymitch, he knew the whole time.
He was taunting me.

1171
01:41:19,282 --> 01:41:21,785
- No, Haymitch. They're in there.
- No, we don't know that.

1172
01:41:21,868 --> 01:41:25,663
Did I lose them both tonight?

1173
01:41:25,747 --> 01:41:27,707
Did I lose them both tonight?

1174
01:41:28,208 --> 01:41:33,421
Did I lose them? I lost them both. No! No!

1175
01:41:42,388 --> 01:41:43,598
There's no news.

1176
01:41:45,892 --> 01:41:47,268
I'm sorry.

1177
01:41:50,355 --> 01:41:52,607
It's the worst torture in the world.

1178
01:41:54,859 --> 01:41:57,862
Waiting, when you know
there's nothing you can do.

1179
01:42:03,326 --> 01:42:05,703
Especially for people like us.

1180
01:42:06,621 --> 01:42:11,167
But whatever strength, courage,

1181
01:42:11,918 --> 01:42:13,336
madness,

1182
01:42:14,420 --> 01:42:17,882
keeps us going,
you find it, at times like these.

1183
01:42:21,010 --> 01:42:22,762
You have it, soldier.

1184
01:42:23,346 --> 01:42:26,182
It's what's kept you alive all this time.

1185
01:42:27,433 --> 01:42:29,352
And it won't fail you now.

1186
01:42:51,708 --> 01:42:52,917
They're back.

1187
01:43:01,509 --> 01:43:03,094
I don't want that.

1188
01:43:07,765 --> 01:43:08,808
Johanna.

1189
01:43:09,267 --> 01:43:10,393
Finnick!

1190
01:43:12,020 --> 01:43:13,354
Finnick!

1191
01:43:13,396 --> 01:43:16,065
Annie? Annie!

1192
01:43:19,986 --> 01:43:22,363
You're safe. You're safe.

1193
01:43:29,537 --> 01:43:30,788
Gale!

1194
01:43:34,083 --> 01:43:35,335
Are you okay?

1195
01:43:36,878 --> 01:43:38,213
What? What is it?

1196
01:43:38,254 --> 01:43:39,380
I don't get it.

1197
01:43:39,714 --> 01:43:43,593
Every gun was back online and on us
and we flew right past them.

1198
01:43:44,260 --> 01:43:45,595
They let us go.

1199
01:43:51,142 --> 01:43:52,352
He's in there.

1200
01:43:54,604 --> 01:43:57,899
Gas we used on the guards knocked
him out, too, but it's wearing off now.

1201
01:44:00,318 --> 01:44:02,153
You should be there when he wakes up.

1202
01:44:07,325 --> 01:44:08,743
Thank you.

1203
01:44:11,871 --> 01:44:13,206
Thank you.

1204
01:44:33,351 --> 01:44:34,727
Peeta.

1205
01:45:08,636 --> 01:45:09,887
Peeta!

1206
01:45:10,513 --> 01:45:13,725
Peeta! Get off! Get off of her!

1207
01:45:14,142 --> 01:45:15,309
Let go!

1208
01:45:50,470 --> 01:45:52,680
No, Katniss. No, you're swollen.
Don't touch.

1209
01:45:53,014 --> 01:45:56,267
No, no, no. Calm down. You're okay.

1210
01:45:59,228 --> 01:46:00,605
Tell her she's awake.

1211
01:46:02,982 --> 01:46:06,319
Don't try to talk. Peeta's okay. I promise.

1212
01:46:07,487 --> 01:46:09,030
I just had to get him off you.

1213
01:46:15,912 --> 01:46:18,039
It's called hijacking.

1214
01:46:19,332 --> 01:46:22,293
We don't know how long
the Capitol's been doing this to Peeta.

1215
01:46:23,252 --> 01:46:26,798
It's fear conditioning.
Enhanced with tracker jacker venom.

1216
01:46:27,507 --> 01:46:29,592
You were stung your first Games.
Remember?

1217
01:46:30,635 --> 01:46:33,721
The venom puts the subject
in a dissociative state.

1218
01:46:34,555 --> 01:46:36,599
And they torture him.

1219
01:46:38,059 --> 01:46:41,729
With shocks and beatings,
and strip down his identity.

1220
01:46:41,771 --> 01:46:44,649
And then all of that suffering and fear
is redirected.

1221
01:46:44,774 --> 01:46:48,361
Associated with other memories
or a person.

1222
01:46:49,821 --> 01:46:51,447
They can change his memories of Katniss?

1223
01:46:51,989 --> 01:46:53,349
To make her seem life-threatening.

1224
01:46:54,951 --> 01:46:57,078
They turned him into a weapon, Katniss.

1225
01:46:58,121 --> 01:46:59,497
To kill you.

1226
01:47:00,915 --> 01:47:01,958
But you can reverse it?

1227
01:47:02,125 --> 01:47:04,085
The fear is the most difficult thing
to overcome.

1228
01:47:04,127 --> 01:47:06,754
We're hardwired to remember fear best.

1229
01:47:06,921 --> 01:47:08,339
It's new terrain.

1230
01:47:09,799 --> 01:47:11,884
But we've put together a team.

1231
01:47:12,844 --> 01:47:14,846
I'm optimistic.

1232
01:47:41,456 --> 01:47:42,707
Good evening.

1233
01:47:44,041 --> 01:47:48,963
Yesterday, I authorized a covert
rescue mission inside the Capitol.

1234
01:47:49,422 --> 01:47:51,966
I am pleased to announce

1235
01:47:52,175 --> 01:47:55,136
that the Victors have been liberated!

1236
01:48:01,642 --> 01:48:05,646
<i>Let this day mark an historic change.</i>

1237
01:48:06,647 --> 01:48:10,026
<i>With The Mockingjay
and the Victors beside us,</i>

1238
01:48:10,067 --> 01:48:13,529
<i>we have sent a clear
message to the Capitol.</i>

1239
01:48:13,779 --> 01:48:17,408
That we will never again endure injustice.

1240
01:48:23,247 --> 01:48:28,002
Today, a day on which we reunited family,

1241
01:48:28,294 --> 01:48:30,963
friends, and loved ones.

1242
01:48:31,756 --> 01:48:35,509
<i>Let all of Panem come together.</i>

1243
01:48:36,636 --> 01:48:40,514
<i>Not to battle
for the amusement of the Capitol.</i>

1244
01:48:40,556 --> 01:48:43,559
<i>But to join hands in this fight.</i>

1245
01:48:50,483 --> 01:48:53,152
Let today be the day we promise

1246
01:48:53,194 --> 01:48:56,948
never to give up, never to give in

1247
01:48:56,989 --> 01:49:00,034
until we have made a new Panem,

1248
01:49:00,076 --> 01:49:03,871
where leaders are elected,
not imposed upon us.

1249
01:49:04,539 --> 01:49:09,001
And where the districts are free
to share the fruits of their labors

1250
01:49:09,043 --> 01:49:11,379
and not fight one another for scraps!

1251
01:49:24,642 --> 01:49:26,561
This new Panem is on the horizon.

1252
01:49:27,019 --> 01:49:29,105
But we must take it for ourselves.

1253
01:49:30,189 --> 01:49:34,527
<i>The road there
leads through the sharp mountains</i>

1254
01:49:34,568 --> 01:49:37,738
<i>and deep ravines of District 2.</i>

1255
01:49:37,780 --> 01:49:42,576
<i>There in the heart of Panem's
steepest mountain range lies</i>

1256
01:49:42,618 --> 01:49:45,830
the Capitol's principal military facility.

1257
01:49:46,872 --> 01:49:49,250
<i>We can conquer this stronghold</i>

1258
01:49:49,875 --> 01:49:52,753
because we are one people,

1259
01:49:53,045 --> 01:49:56,590
one army, one voice.

1260
01:49:56,716 --> 01:50:01,262
<i>Because today is our new beginning.</i>

1261
01:50:01,387 --> 01:50:05,558
Today we have freed the Victors.

1262
01:50:06,058 --> 01:50:09,145
Tomorrow, Panem!

1263
01:50:17,236 --> 01:50:21,616
Hoorah! Hoorah! Hoorah!

